{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"b47f6821c6b7fb573a49b44bef9a128e24a33fd3088e2764508d4f602f5936a3","command":{"allowed_records":[],"directive":"T1-1e5dd5448a7c0d38","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"Authorization is **OPTIONAL** for MCP implementations. When supported:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t1_o1","terms":["authorization optionality","MCP implementations"]},{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"implements a selected subset of their features to ensure security and interoperability","kind":"observe","local_id":"t1_o2","terms":["subset of OAuth specs","simplicity vs interoperability"]},{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"- [OAuth 2.1 IETF DRAFT](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-12)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t1_o3","terms":["OAuth 2.1 draft dependency"]},{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"MCP auth implementations **MUST** implement OAuth 2.1 with appropriate security","kind":"observe","local_id":"t1_o4","terms":["OAuth 2.1 mandatory for auth implementations"]},{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"MCP servers **SHOULD** support the OAuth grant types that best align with the intended","kind":"observe","local_id":"t1_o5","terms":["grant type selection","server discretion"]},{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"MCP servers that do not support the OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server Metadata protocol,","kind":"observe","local_id":"t1_o7","terms":["metadata fallback requirement"]},{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"MCP clients _SHOULD_ include the header `MCP-Protocol-Version: <protocol-version>` during","kind":"observe","local_id":"t1_o8","terms":["protocol version header","discovery"]},{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"The authorization base URL **MUST** be determined from the MCP server URL by discarding","kind":"observe","local_id":"t1_o9","terms":["authorization base URL derivation"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t1_o2","t1_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t1_c2","object":"OAuth 2.1 draft, RFC8414, RFC7591","predicate":"is a selected subset of","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP authorization standards basis","text":"The mechanism is based on OAuth 2.1 IETF draft, RFC8414 and RFC7591 but implements only a selected subset of their features for security, interoperability and simplicity."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t1_o4","t1_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t1_c3","object":"OAuth 2.1 MUST, RFC7591 SHOULD, RFC8414 client MUST/server SHOULD","predicate":"mandates/recommends","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP auth implementation requirements","text":"MCP auth implementations MUST implement OAuth 2.1 with security measures for confidential and public clients; DCR is SHOULD; AS metadata is MUST for clients and SHOULD for servers."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t1_o7","t1_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t1_c4","object":"fallback default endpoints and root-level base URL","predicate":"requires","stance":"reported","subject":"metadata discovery fallback","text":"Servers lacking Authorization Server Metadata MUST support fallback default URLs; the authorization base URL MUST be derived by discarding the MCP server URL path."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t1_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t1_c6","object":"MCP-Protocol-Version header","predicate":"recommends","stance":"reported","subject":"metadata discovery header","text":"Clients SHOULD send MCP-Protocol-Version during Server Metadata Discovery so servers can respond per protocol version; example value 2024-11-05."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t1_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t1_c7","object":"server choice per audience","predicate":"is left open to","stance":"open","subject":"OAuth grant type support","text":"Which grant types an MCP server supports is left to server discretion, aligned to intended audience (authorization code vs client credentials)."},{"about":["OAuth 2.1 draft dependency","staleness"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t1_q1","needed":"check draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-12 status and any version-pinning language elsewhere in the document","text":"Does the spec pin a specific OAuth 2.1 draft version, and what happens if that draft changes or is superseded?"},{"about":["subset scope","limitations"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t1_q2","needed":"scan remaining sections for explicit exclusions or non-goals","text":"Which OAuth features were excluded from the 'selected subset', and are those exclusions documented as limitations?"},{"about":["protocol version","staleness"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t1_q3","needed":"compare against later MCP spec revisions","text":"Is the MCP-Protocol-Version header value 2024-11-05 current, or has it been superseded by a later protocol version?"},{"about":["alternative transports","open requirement"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t1_q4","needed":"check whether any companion document enumerates them","text":"What security best practices are required for alternative (non-HTTP, non-STDIO) transports?"},{"based_on":["t1_o3","t1_o4"],"falsifier":"A statement in the document pinning the draft as stable or a later revision adopting the final RFC without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t1_h1","text":"Because the spec builds on an IETF draft rather than a final RFC, its OAuth 2.1 requirements are provisional and may be qualified once the draft is finalized."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d"],"ranges":[["d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d",0,5880]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"a59970ed3403c61b4ea0fd10b65faa0e5acba5e