{"doc_id":"d_0b1e9103fea8fa5ef272198e7fcb3c264c0d113b3cb79352242dd7fd7884d30d","exact_quote":"S->>C: 404 Not Found","kind":"observe","local_id":"t5_o7","terms":["discovery failure","fallback trigger"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t5_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t5_c1","object":"HTTP transports; STDIO uses environment credentials","predicate":"is limited to","stance":"reported","subject":"authorization flow scope","text":"The spec's authorization flow is scoped to HTTP-based transports; STDIO implementations instead retrieve credentials from the environment."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t5_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t5_c2","object":"HTTP 401 Unauthorized","predicate":"MUST receive","stance":"reported","subject":"unauthenticated requests","text":"Servers MUST respond with HTTP 401 Unauthorized when authorization is required and not yet proven by the client."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t5_o3","t5_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t5_c3","object":"OAuth 2.1 public-client PKCE flow","predicate":"demonstrates","stance":"reported","subject":"authorization code example","text":"The authorization code example demonstrates OAuth 2.1 for public clients using PKCE, with the client sending code plus code_verifier in the token request."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t5_o6","t5_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t5_c5","object":"well-known GET, 404 triggers fallback","predicate":"proceeds via","stance":"reported","subject":"metadata discovery flow","text":"Clients discover server metadata by GETting /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server; on 404 they fall back to default endpoints."},{"based_on":["t5_o3"],"falsifier":"Text pinning draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-12 as final/stable, or a revision adopting the final RFC without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t5_h1","text":"The spec's reliance on OAuth 2.1 IETF draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-12 leaves its MUST-implement OAuth 2.1 requirement provisional until that draft is finalized."},{"about":["metadata discovery","fallback conditions"],"