{"body":{"actor":"w2","audit_root":"d1989bc0574db4de67ffa849b1c502ae850050caed33b96d1ebdbe326bd1a32e","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","388fc430f833e291a33eab7b8ffd612a54d4fd2510b7ef35c0599632ac25fd0a","78efa91808f3890df1f708ce3e17b6a140fe9bf7604c5411124d37a266b60e6d","b66101f3e4eb0513dd15f5fd70f11c0ff5fc120574e1a224a94652eb7539fed3","b8aad0c9bc884c02e8997d480c042678fc10115174d50419ee348c40bdddacba","e081d0bb592a36e3829ee13f994ca94ba591f281a6186f4fd9b5aec786ffb024","f111d8ab28f0e51c88d7863c6ab1f2dff608c218e36d150d405bbfc4811e72b7","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd","fa57fb9a313bdb46c473b885ad58c039022aa4190b7d77e279b4d2cd1ebbec81"],"directive":"T9-f512b13bfb8d6e45","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804","exact_quote":"1. First, closing the input stream to the child process (the server)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t9_o1","terms":["stdio shutdown step 1","closing input stream"]},{"doc_id":"d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804","exact_quote":"2. Waiting for the server to exit, or sending `SIGTERM` if the server does not exit","kind":"observe","local_id":"t9_o2","terms":["stdio shutdown step 2","SIGTERM escalation"]},{"doc_id":"d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804","exact_quote":"3. Sending `SIGKILL` if the server does not exit within a reasonable time after `SIGTERM`","kind":"observe","local_id":"t9_o3","terms":["stdio shutdown step 3","SIGKILL escalation","undefined reasonable time"]},{"doc_id":"d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804","exact_quote":"Implementations **SHOULD** establish timeouts for all sent requests, to prevent hung","kind":"observe","local_id":"t9_o6","terms":["request timeouts","hung connections"]},{"doc_id":"d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804","exact_quote":"Implementations **MAY** choose to reset the timeout clock when receiving a [progress","kind":"observe","local_id":"t9_o8","terms":["progress resets timeout clock"]},{"doc_id":"d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804","exact_quote":"Implementations **SHOULD** be prepared to handle these error cases:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t9_o11","terms":["error cases: version mismatch, capability negotiation, timeouts"]},{"doc_id":"d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804","exact_quote":"\"supported\": [\"2024-11-05\"],","kind":"observe","local_id":"t9_o12","terms":["example lists only 2024-11-05 as supported version"]},{"doc_id":"d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804","exact_quote":"For the stdio [transport](/specification/2025-03-26/basic/transports), the client **SHOULD** initiate","kind":"observe","local_id":"t9_o13","terms":["client-initiated stdio shutdown"]},{"as_of":20250326,"based_on":["t9_o13","t9_o1","t9_o2","t9_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t9_c1","object":"closing input, waiting, SIGTERM, then SIGKILL","predicate":"SHOULD initiate by","stance":"reported","subject":"stdio client shutdown","text":"For stdio, the client SHOULD initiate shutdown by closing the child's input stream, waiting, then sending SIGTERM and finally SIGKILL if the server has not exited."},{"as_of":20250326,"based_on":["t9_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t9_c4","object":"timeouts","predicate":"SHOULD establish","stance":"reported","subject":"sent requests","text":"Implementations SHOULD establish timeouts for all sent requests to prevent hung connections and resource exhaustion."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t9_o12"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t9_c9","object":"2024-11-05 only","predicate":"lists supported versions","stance":"unknown","subject":"initialization error example","text":"The initialization error example lists only 2024-11-05 as supported, which predates the 2025-03-26 revision this section belongs to; its relevance to current versions is not stated."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t9_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t9_c10","object":"a reasonable time","predicate":"is left unspecified as","stance":"open","subject":"stdio escalation timing","text":"The stdio escalation timing is left as 'a reasonable time' with no defined value, so the wait before SIGTERM and SIGKILL remains unspecified."},{"about":["@388fc430f833e291","@b66101f3e4eb0513"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t9_q1","needed":"Check the lifecycle or shutdown sections of later MCP specification revisions for any application-level shutdown message.","text":"The section gives transport-level shutdown procedures but no rationale for omitting an application-level shutdown message, and it does not say whether later revisions added one."},{"about":["@e081d0bb592a36e3"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t9_q2","needed":"Check the initialization or lifecycle section of the same 2025-03-26 revision for the disconnect guidance.","text":"The section says implementations SHOULD be prepared to handle protocol version mismatch but does not state that clients must disconnect."},{"about":["t9_c10","t9_c4"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t9_q3","needed":"Check the SDK or utilities documentation and other sections of the spec for recommended timeout values.","text":"No numeric default or range is given for request timeouts or the stdio 'reasonable time', so the open limitation on timeout values remains."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804"],"ranges":[["d_0d6aa094546300c922e9f888e59a2a42387e1ab9eb3a5eba2887add9eaae4804",5980,7942]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"d9db17ccf56969454e8af0a6319fec0d81e2704299ef3526eae56a03ed52efba","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["e2dedef89f831d0bc35b7f5ee474c6c8f89fdadb371943e8d56e0c1d71469f1d","4fb8c405050f2c767b17420f6c321be48f7b368ebefd771118dadc6c49f9a8db","19e9c33ce54ac9a669f08