{"body":{"actor":"w2","audit_root":"81724ef5a955a0273237e133499fac90269839774fcb370630efe354e3296cc2","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","931a61a051ec316ffbe720982ea9d05243d14af58d333910026e7d46ea12de5e","b397efe27e1ba0b3ddc96d0747b439a4fecc819c2ed2e231a98376466b66ac60","b7a5eb5e2373eea5ed723c57c6f9a195eed001f7ab1b346a0c70eb65c3692d9b","bd8ca52f7fecf3cec5bfb7fa53eeae7bcfc1b0496f6c2eef31a8f0043e0a1ab2","d686aac174d904fa6d1ad232ef834c3677c20312dd90bc4cf6dde0d2b49c457d","dbf5279a837ea8753bd40b6b10151ca3c406fc35274d7c6c62956ceae960e69c","e2ee9a90754d400ec44e3df92d921f1f2cb06dc0649cfa6d5257ae2f09a302a4","e38ed2520ced46d2f428362c62b287e94ffd1b32591fd4f777ab694d03ab4029","ee0d6b8cf2a71b56c4634c7f2157c016e6b75ef5c16f4b0d8c5ee5a46e0e0f4d","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"TR18-0a0c250a9aa7bf72","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"the client **MUST** include the `MCP-Protocol-Version:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o1","terms":["client must send protocol version header on HTTP requests"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"The protocol version sent by the client **SHOULD** be the one","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o2","terms":["protocol version header should match negotiated version"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"it **MUST** respond with `400 Bad Request`.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o4","terms":["invalid or unsupported protocol version gets 400"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"**Servers** wanting to support older clients should:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o6","terms":["server guidance for backwards compatibility"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"If it succeeds, the client can assume this is a server supporting the new Streamable","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o7","terms":["client detection of Streamable HTTP server via InitializeRequest"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"If it fails with an HTTP 4xx status code (e.g., 405 Method Not Allowed or 404 Not","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o8","terms":["client fallback on 4xx failure of initialization"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"When the `endpoint` event arrives, the client can assume this is a server running","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o9","terms":["client detection of old HTTP+SSE server via endpoint event"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"Clients and servers **MAY** implement additional custom transport mechanisms to suit","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o10","terms":["custom transports are optional"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"**SHOULD** document their specific connection establishment and message exchange patterns","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o12","terms":["custom transports should document connection patterns"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"maintain backwards compatibility with the deprecated [HTTP+SSE","kind":"observe","local_id":"t18_o13","terms":["HTTP+SSE transport deprecated"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t18_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t18_c1","object":"MCP-Protocol-Version header","predicate":"MUST include","stance":"reported","subject":"client HTTP requests","text":"Clients MUST include the MCP-Protocol-Version header on all subsequent HTTP requests to the server."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t18_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t18_c2","object":"version negotiated during initialization","predicate":"SHOULD be","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP-Protocol-Version header value","text":"The protocol version sent by clients SHOULD be the version negotiated during initialization."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t18_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t18_c4","object":"400 Bad Request","predicate":"MUST respond with","stance":"reported","subject":"invalid or unsupported protocol version","text":"A server receiving an invalid or unsupported MCP-Protocol-Version MUST respond with 400 Bad Request."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t18_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t18_c7","object":"server supports Streamable HTTP transport","predicate":"can assume","stance":"reported","subject":"client InitializeRequest POST","text":"If a client's InitializeRequest POST succeeds, the client can assume the server supports the Streamable HTTP transport."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t18_o8","t18_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t18_c8","object":"old HTTP+SSE transport after endpoint event","predicate":"should use","stance":"reported","subject":"client fallback after HTTP 4xx","text":"If the InitializeRequest POST fails with an HTTP 4xx, the client issues a GET expecting an endpoint event; on its arrival the client uses the old HTTP+SSE transport."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t18_o13"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t18_c9","object":"deprecated","predicate":"is","stance":"superseded","subject":"HTTP+SSE transport (2024-11-05)","text":"The HTTP+SSE transport from protocol version 2024-11-05 is deprecated; the spec keeps it only for backwards compatibility."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t18_o10","t18_o12"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t18_c11","object":"connection establishment and message exchange patterns","predicate":"SHOULD document","stance":"reported","subject":"custom transports","text":"Custom transports SHOULD document their specific connection establishment and message exchange patterns."},{"about":["client fallback between Streamable HTTP and HTTP+SSE"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t18_q1","needed":"Check the lifecycle and transports sections for failure handling outside this section.","text":"The section gives client fallback only for HTTP 4xx failures of InitializeRequest. Behaviour on other failures (e.g., 5xx or no endpoint event) is left open here."},{"about":["default protocol version for servers"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t18_q2","needed":"Check the lifecycle version-negotiation section for how the negotiated version is stored and used.","text":"Whether the 2025-03-26 default applies when the server has the negotiated version from initialization is not settled by this section beyond the 'no other way to identify' condition."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b"],"ranges":[["d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b",11113,13956]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"d493b125e7ef3ad07dad7a146a89f6ff8f95788b68261e8e468c06cc0dfcf2f8","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["6b97dc008b4a6cd0521c161c66bf64a4fe87589c54e638c26ea57ddb53b5a74f","506a6f2b61632db5b3363dfea53797566a45b155488f7439b72a0d25b8026286","78e447a41b1070ada3555411e748cb0c89febf3f2bc0b7759bf84137a87dd680","8dac8416f0e91e912aafc5b4a50d35354993741311ef9ab0fb03e8372fb80ca7","9783b7b3f2641adb8d3c2836cb071ba9ed1c713701858e85f2a63e0bdd0b2213","2e86c7bfd0c75df14e8740d9ca733712cb45ce0b3d20d779ec7023c1b363bb56","eadd8afe69ca1427d0aee4c4b7f59f3e5e3eb53372bdafaa13dfe1434127180d","0c69a23666ecbd010e39683e565ab103ac21c988ea1803f132d3e1f32e1ed108","a845d581b92670a5c70bccee041ab56b955570910ca61b2d046c171a6271dd94","b561abdb788b8ca7c963b85f4bb821b3b88fbbead212d5ed2334fc864b0d83f4","4ee07bfe7ee7c2e5237f68e6390e4b02424494e2ef3aca3719d323efc20ba006","fe27cb6695688e6e9791ab15a1b2bcb69f595cd0870de07569a28121478ccd22","11cfe676ee899222137feb55fb64a48232b47ee5c19ce0533c1986dd4471424f","9aba4a5d947b220887aa17e578ce5a00d7a9ae1745c1611c6a9f5b5c8a2aa742"