{"body":{"actor":"w4","audit_root":"d911c5582afe04196cb25c5181dddb9e7e1a98895b5b7e90860ec7321c1984c3","command":{"allowed_records":["055c3b232f4d91ca3898c658c421637b3ec6181635f6eec74ea53ca4449c86b5","0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","c8433f8a1df56a4154b6dd2ad7ffe98151da3db1f9ef0f33bcb40ad5bcf420ac","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T22-075e69133a5a150f","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"MCP servers **MUST** implement one of the following discovery mechanisms to provide authorization server location information to MCP clients:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o1","terms":["MCP servers","discovery mechanisms","authorization server location"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t22_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t22_c1","object":"one of two discovery mechanisms to provide authorization server location information","predicate":"MUST implement","stance":"qualified","subject":"MCP servers","text":"MCP servers MUST implement at least one discovery mechanism (WWW-Authenticate Header or Well-Known URI) to provide authorization server location info."},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"MCP clients **MUST** support both discovery mechanisms and use the resource metadata URL from the parsed `WWW-Authenticate` headers when present;","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o2","terms":["MCP clients","discovery mechanisms","WWW-Authenticate headers"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"otherwise, they **MUST** fall back to constructing and requesting the well-known URIs in the order listed above.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o3","terms":["MCP clients","well-known URIs","fallback order"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t22_o2","t22_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t22_c2","object":"both discovery mechanisms with mandated fallback order","predicate":"MUST support","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP clients","text":"MCP clients MUST support both discovery mechanisms, using parsed WWW-Authenticate headers first and falling back to well-known URIs."},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Clients **MUST NOT** assume any particular set relationship between the challenged\nscope set and `scopes_supported`.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o5","terms":["clients","scope set relationship","scopes_supported"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Clients **MUST** treat the scopes provided in the\nchallenge as authoritative for satisfying the current request.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o6","terms":["clients","challenge scopes","authoritative"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t22_o5","t22_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t22_c4","object":"challenge scopes as authoritative without assuming set relationship to scopes_supported","predicate":"MUST treat","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP clients scope interpretation","text":"Clients MUST NOT assume any set relationship between challenged scopes and scopes_supported, but MUST treat challenge scopes as authoritative."},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Servers **SHOULD** strive for\nconsistency in how they construct scope sets but they are not required to surface every dynamically\nissued scope through `scopes_supported`.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o7","terms":["servers","scope consistency","dynamic scopes"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t22_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t22_c5","object":"every dynamically issued scope through scopes_supported","predicate":"is not required for","stance":"qualified","subject":"server scope surfacing","text":"Servers are not required to surface every dynamically issued scope in scopes_supported, qualifying the general consistency recommendation."},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"MCP clients **MUST** be able to parse `WWW-Authenticate` headers and respond appropriately to `HTTP 401 Unauthorized` responses from the MCP server.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o8","terms":["MCP clients","WWW-Authenticate parsing","HTTP 401 Unauthorized"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t22_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t22_c6","object":"WWW-Authenticate headers in HTTP 401 Unauthorized responses","predicate":"MUST parse and respond to","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP clients","text":"MCP clients MUST parse WWW-Authenticate headers and respond appropriately to HTTP 401 Unauthorized responses."},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"If the `scope` parameter is absent, clients **SHOULD** apply the fallback behavior defined in the [Scope Selection Strategy](#scope-selection-strategy) section.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o9","terms":["scope parameter absent","client fallback","Scope Selection Strategy"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t22_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t22_c7","object":"fallback behavior defined in Scope Selection Strategy section","predicate":"SHOULD apply","stance":"qualified","subject":"client behavior on absent scope parameter","text":"When the scope parameter is absent in WWW-Authenticate, clients SHOULD apply the fallback behavior in Scope Selection Strategy."},{"about":["Scope Selection Strategy","absent scope fallback"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t22_q1","needed":"Examine the Scope Selection Strategy section in document d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54.","text":"What fallback behavior is specified in Scope Selection Strategy when the WWW-Authenticate header omits the scope parameter?"},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"MCP clients **MUST** attempt multiple well-known endpoints when discovering authorization server metadata.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o10","terms":["MCP clients","authorization server metadata discovery","well-known endpoints"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"For issuer URLs with path components (e.g., `https://auth.example.com/tenant1`), clients **MUST** try endpoints in the following priority order:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o11","terms":["issuer URLs with path components","priority order"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"For issuer URLs without path components (e.g., `https://auth.example.com`), clients **MUST** try:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t22_o12","terms":["issuer URLs without path components","discovery priority"]}],"scope":{"docs":["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54"],"ranges":[["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54",5106,9360]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"97fbe7564d99771181562c69ff5c1a343e0b606c0cc53532a499de119c7497fd","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["fe51abf1054dd84b78c9c3c2401616daa99f1b7fbac85ff6e764ce25654d823b","56f25361d7b21147dcacd05766d15513c201c7a4e3b770601ce515b1d02488b3","b1eb5911128212173a40b1c991c4bb5041860000a2d2fe445f5f06b03c3a7c9c","d902b66471ee70660924bd195029f2b274f5af7122d7f8b616a7c45e05d2ef33","656fd3bf723830f272632d3eb5115f739eb5839bda4515885b18