{"body":{"actor":"w2","audit_root":"37b55bc117f2356f6067a8c03d0d6b73cfa4b8e5020b016152d46b9c7d56a250","command":{"allowed_records":["055c3b232f4d91ca3898c658c421637b3ec6181635f6eec74ea53ca4449c86b5","0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","c8433f8a1df56a4154b6dd2ad7ffe98151da3db1f9ef0f33bcb40ad5bcf420ac","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T26-b2ef0bb4cf419634","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"MCP servers **MUST** validate that tokens presented to them were specifically issued for their use","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o1","terms":["token audience validation by servers"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"audiences **when the Authorization Server supports the capability**. To enable current and future adoption:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o2","terms":["RFC 8707 audience binding is conditional on AS support"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Authorization servers **SHOULD** issue short-lived access tokens to reduce the impact of leaked tokens.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o3","terms":["short-lived access tokens as a recommendation"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"MCP clients **MUST** use the `S256` code challenge method when technically capable","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o5","terms":["S256 PKCE method conditional on technical capability"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Since OAuth 2.1 and PKCE specifications do not define a mechanism for clients to discover PKCE support","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o6","terms":["no standard PKCE discovery mechanism"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"If the field is absent, MCP clients **MUST** refuse to proceed.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o7","terms":["fail-closed when code_challenge_methods_supported is absent"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Authorization servers providing OpenID Connect Discovery 1.0 **MUST** include `code_challenge_methods_supported` in their metadata to ensure MCP compatibility.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o8","terms":["OIDC providers must publish code_challenge_methods_supported"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"MCP clients **SHOULD** use and verify state parameters in the authorization code flow","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o9","terms":["state parameter verification as a recommendation"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Authorization servers **SHOULD** only automatically redirect the user agent if it trusts the redirection URI.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o10","terms":["automatic redirect only to trusted URIs"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"If the URI is not trusted, the authorization server MAY inform the user and rely on the user to make the correct decision.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o11","terms":["optional user prompt for untrusted redirect"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Authorization servers fetching metadata documents **SHOULD** consider","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o12","terms":["SSRF consideration for metadata fetching as a recommendation"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"A malicious client could use this to trigger the authorization server to make requests to arbitrary URLs,","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o13","terms":["SSRF risk from client-supplied metadata URLs"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"All redirect URIs **MUST** be either `localhost` or use HTTPS.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o14","terms":["redirect URI scheme requirement"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Clients and servers **MUST** implement secure token storage and follow OAuth best practices,","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o15","terms":["secure token storage obligation"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"The authorization server takes a URL as input from an unknown client and fetches that URL.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o16","terms":["client-supplied URL fetched by authorization server"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"does not define `code_challenge_methods_supported`, this field is commonly included by OpenID providers.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o17","terms":["OIDC metadata does not define the PKCE field"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o2","t26_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c1","object":"when AS supports the capability","predicate":"provides benefit","stance":"qualified","subject":"RFC 8707 token audience binding","text":"RFC 8707 audience binding of tokens is a benefit only when the Authorization Server supports the capability; server validation of audience is stated as an unconditional MUST."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c2","object":"authorization servers","predicate":"should be issued by","stance":"qualified","subject":"short-lived access tokens","text":"Issuing short-lived access tokens is a SHOULD for authorization servers, not a MUST."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c4","object":"MCP clients when technically capable","predicate":"MUST be used by","stance":"qualified","subject":"S256 code challenge method","text":"The S256 PKCE challenge method is required only when the client is technically capable of using it."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o6","t26_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c5","object":"code_challenge_methods_supported metadata","predicate":"is inferred from","stance":"open","subject":"PKCE support discovery","text":"The section admits PKCE support cannot be discovered directly and instead requires clients to infer support from metadata, refusing to proceed when the field is absent."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o8","t26_o17"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c6","object":"code_challenge_methods_supported","predicate":"must include","stance":"open","subject":"OpenID Connect provider metadata","text":"Because the OpenID Provider Metadata does not define code_challenge_methods_supported, the section's MUST on OIDC providers depends on a field outside the cited specification."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c7","object":"MCP clients","predicate":"SHOULD be used and verified by","stance":"qualified","subject":"state parameter verification","text":"Clients verifying state parameters is a SHOULD, not a MUST, in the authorization code flow."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o10","t26_o11"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c8","object":"trusted redirection URIs","predicate":"SHOULD occur only for","stance":"qualified","subject":"automatic redirect of user agent","text":"Automatic redirection is limited to trusted URIs as a SHOULD; for untrusted URIs the server MAY prompt the user instead."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o12","t26_o16"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c9","object":"authorization servers fetching metadata documents","predicate":"SHOULD be considered by","stance":"open","subject":"SSRF protection for metadata fetching","text":"SSRF protection for metadata fetching is only a SHOULD and is delegated to the referenced draft's guidance rather than specified here."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o14"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c10","object":"localhost or HTTPS","predicate":"MUST be","stance":"reported","subject":"redirect URIs","text":"Redirect URIs must be localhost or use HTTPS."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o15"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c11","object":"clients and servers","predicate":"MUST be implemented by","stance":"reported","subject":"token storage","text":"Clients and servers must implement secure token storage and follow OAuth best practices."},{"about":["OAuth 2.1 draft dependence","Client ID Metadata Document draft dependence"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t26_q1","needed":"Check later revisions of this section and the final RFC or draft status of the referenced documents.","text":"Will the cited IETF drafts (draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13 and draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document-00) be finalized, and will the cited sections keep the same requirements?"},{"about":["PKCE discovery gap","OIDC code_challenge_methods_supported"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t26_q2","needed":"Check the PKCE and Authorization Server Metadata subsection in later spec revisions and the OIDC provider metadata specification.","text":"Will a standard PKCE discovery mechanism or an OIDC requirement for code_challenge_methods_supported be added, closing the open gap in PKCE discovery?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54"],"ranges":[["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c085