{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"f2042d7218dffbc7e3936056a796d85df892a9c05dafdb8c6614b4bd0753e2a5","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T32-f5258f08f497b736","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"Intermediate servers that do not recognize an `Mcp-Param-{Name}` header\n**MUST** forward it and otherwise ignore it, as required by the\n[HTTP Semantics RFC][http-semantics].","kind":"observe","local_id":"t32_o4","terms":["intermediaries","forwarding","HTTP Semantics RFC"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"When validating integer parameter values, servers **SHOULD** compare the\nheader value and the body value numerically rather than as strings (e.g.,\n`42.0` and `42` are considered equal).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t32_o7","terms":["integer validation","numeric comparison","SHOULD"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"header indicates a version that requires header–body validation. If the\nversion is older or the header is absent, the intermediary **SHOULD** reject\nthe request rather than trusting unvalidated header values.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t32_o9","terms":["intermediary policy","MCP-Protocol-Version","unvalidated headers"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t32_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t32_c3","object":"intermediate servers","predicate":"MUST be forwarded and otherwise ignored by","stance":"reported","subject":"unrecognized Mcp-Param-{Name} headers","text":"Intermediaries that do not recognize an Mcp-Param-{Name} header MUST forward it and otherwise ignore it, per the HTTP Semantics RFC."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t32_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t32_c6","object":"servers","predicate":"SHOULD be compared numerically by","stance":"qualified","subject":"integer parameter header validation","text":"When validating integer parameter values, servers SHOULD compare header and body values numerically rather than as strings, so 42.0 and 42 are equal."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t32_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t32_c8","object":"requests with older or absent MCP-Protocol-Version","predicate":"SHOULD verify version and reject","stance":"qualified","subject":"intermediary policy on mirrored headers","text":"Intermediaries enforcing policy on mirrored headers SHOULD verify MCP-Protocol-Version requires header-body validation, and SHOULD reject when the version is older or the header absent."},{"based_on":["t32_o3","t32_o7","t32_o9"],"falsifier":"A later revision stating these SHOULD items as unconditional MUST requirements without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t32_h1","text":"The SHOULD-level items here (numeric integer comparison, intermediary version-check rejection, client tools/list retry) are optionality that later revisions could tighten to MUST."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530"],"ranges":[["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530",20841,26565]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"f2e28632ee7a863723c908d1029eb34d9a66a3f22664fb5e1