{"body":{"actor":"w3","audit_root":"c1f46f0696644e825cb8526ba7851858afd400edd8b3e2a6e99cbbc488865c3f","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T30-50553a505204a44a","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"Every POST request to the MCP endpoint **MUST** include an\n`MCP-Protocol-Version` header.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t30_o1","terms":["protocol version header","POST requests","MCP endpoint"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t30_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t30_c1","object":"every POST request to the MCP endpoint","predicate":"MUST be included in","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP-Protocol-Version header","text":"Every POST request to the MCP endpoint is required to include an MCP-Protocol-Version header."},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"If the values do not match, the server **MUST** reject the request\nwith `400 Bad Request` and a `HeaderMismatch` JSON-RPC error","kind":"observe","local_id":"t30_o2","terms":["header mismatch","server rejection","HeaderMismatch error"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t30_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t30_c2","object":"HTTP 400 Bad Request with a HeaderMismatch JSON-RPC error when mismatched","predicate":"MUST cause","stance":"reported","subject":"protocol-version header and body metadata","text":"A mismatch between the protocol-version header and body metadata requires rejection with HTTP 400 and a HeaderMismatch JSON-RPC error."},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"If the server does not implement the requested RPC method, it **MUST** respond\nwith `404 Not Found` and a JSON-RPC error with code `-32601`","kind":"observe","local_id":"t30_o3","terms":["unsupported RPC method","404 response","method not found"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t30_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t30_c3","object":"404 Not Found with JSON-RPC error code -32601","predicate":"MUST receive","stance":"reported","subject":"unimplemented RPC method","text":"Servers must return 404 Not Found with JSON-RPC code -32601 when they do not implement the requested RPC method."},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"These headers are **REQUIRED** for compliance.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t30_o5","terms":["standard request headers","compliance","Mcp-Method","Mcp-Name"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t30_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t30_c5","object":"compliance","predicate":"are REQUIRED for","stance":"reported","subject":"standard request headers","text":"The listed standard request headers are required for compliance."},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"If the `Mcp-Name` source value cannot be safely represented as a plain ASCII\nheader value, clients **MUST** encode it using the Base64 sentinel format","kind":"observe","local_id":"t30_o6","terms":["Mcp-Name","ASCII header values","Base64 encoding"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t30_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t30_c6","object":"the Base64 sentinel format when not safely representable as plain ASCII","predicate":"MUST be encoded using","stance":"reported","subject":"Mcp-Name source value","text":"Clients must use the specified Base64 sentinel format when an Mcp-Name source value cannot safely be represented as plain ASCII."},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"While the use of `x-mcp-header` is optional for servers, clients **MUST**\nsupport this feature.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t30_o7","terms":["x-mcp-header","server optionality","client support"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t30_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t30_c7","object":"clients","predicate":"is optional for servers while support is mandatory for","stance":"qualified","subject":"x-mcp-header extension","text":"The x-mcp-header extension remains optional for servers, but clients are required to support it, leaving server adoption optional."},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"When a server's tool definition includes\n`x-mcp-header` annotations, conforming clients **MUST** mirror the\ndesignated parameter values into HTTP headers.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t30_o8","terms":["x-mcp-header annotations","tool definitions","header mirroring"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t30_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t30_c8","object":"HTTP headers by conforming clients when x-mcp-header annotations are present","predicate":"MUST be mirrored into","stance":"reported","subject":"designated tool parameter values","text":"When x-mcp-header annotations are present in a tool definition, conforming clients must mirror the designated parameter values into HTTP headers."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530"],"ranges":[["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530",10358,14905]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"0fd24eb42fd5611ff0d41fcc3c20f8c59d7b3d0073e0c92756b0346fe9c2936d","outcome":{"kind":"records","result"