{"body":{"actor":"kernel","audit_root":"929eb6f6eadcd47747fcf65d63bdd700e8396881f7f1672e4672bd443a2f9882","command":{"checkpoint":{"context":{"accepted":["@99682737dd21263f","@745eef219a882f5a","@a4f65e73dacec0d5","@9f0370080114342e","@036087b2327c17ec","@b3be67438e6e8355","@ea949c2440167470","@b1c96603ea5c46ae","@3074585250f23807","@aa51e7767ee675da","@822f25e01d8939c8","@b0a23c077eb0f816","@fe4cfbf9711855f8","@b6855b7841ec41df"],"attempt":1,"excluded":[{"index":7,"local_id":"t30_c4","rests_on":"t30_o4"}],"kind":"EXTEND","refused":[{"error":{"code":"QUOTE_NOT_FOUND_IN_BYTES","expected_by_kernel":{"rule":"byte_quote"},"field":"exact_quote","message":"quote has no byte-exact occurrence","obligation":null,"status":"error"},"index":6,"local_id":"t30_o4"}],"task_id":"T30-50553a505204a44a","work_key":"doc:d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530#2"},"from":0,"key":"task-repair:T30-50553a505204a44a:1","to":0},"kind":"batch","operations":[]},"engine_root":"0fd24eb42fd5611ff0d41fcc3c20f8c59d7b3d0073e0c92756b0346fe9c2936d","outcome":{"kind":"value","result":{"accepted_operations":0,"checkpointed":true,"error":null,"failed_index":null,"results":[]}},"request_hash":"700985a84b5b34306b6e0aeec46ce8071510c89720fcd0721ac963935dc3c7e5","submission_id":"T30-50553a505204a44a#repair1"},"hash":"5d0d34f11241fa5307248721588e6aea0915c09836358b385977a37b06b2f822","header":{"body_hash":"804b0ba900cb374a61322e9a5df74c0b6e9506053245a3e3e6c818caa36b613d","format":"sbgk-session-log/3","previous":"bb608b7b85200926c3fb7115b80500d5824c512aef5b9c063ea2a3d1737d8274","records_root":"fe7c90ca2214e168f5ffe6cccb15729c3b8a03c403e48c406441cd589fdd8c41","seq":145,"wal_op":"audit"}}
{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"872a29eaafe9a2ef5e2b9c8b0a66e164f6b208282d415b01c35b9c5d888ec902","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"TR33-a5c79fc8074224f2","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"When constructing a `tools/call` request via HTTP transport, the client","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o1","terms":["client behavior","tools/call","HTTP transport"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"`x-mcp-header` and extract the value at each annotated property's exact","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o2","terms":["x-mcp-header","inputSchema","Mcp-Param headers"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"`Mcp-Param-*` headers are missing or do not match the body, the client","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o3","terms":["HeaderMismatch","client retry","tools/list"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"`400 Bad Request` HTTP status and JSON-RPC error code `-32020`","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o5","terms":["HeaderMismatch error code","400 Bad Request"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"are case-insensitive. Clients and servers **MUST** use case-insensitive","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o6","terms":["case sensitivity","header names"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"different components in the network rely on different sources of truth","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o7","terms":["security rationale","header-body validation"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"header value and the body value numerically rather than as strings (e.g.,","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o8","terms":["integer comparison","SHOULD","validation"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"`400 Bad Request`) for validation failures but are not required to return","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o9","terms":["intermediaries","no JSON-RPC error required"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"version is older or the header is absent, the intermediary **SHOULD** reject","kind":"observe","local_id":"t33o10","terms":["intermediary policy","MCP-Protocol-Version","unvalidated headers"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t33o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t33c1","object":"Mcp-Method and Mcp-Name headers","predicate":"MUST append","stance":"reported","subject":"tools/call request construction over HTTP","text":"Clients constructing tools/call over HTTP MUST extract method, params.name and params.uri from the body and append Mcp-Method and, if applicable, Mcp-Name headers."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t33o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t33c2","object":"Mcp-Param-{Name} headers","predicate":"MUST be mirrored into","stance":"reported","subject":"x-mcp-header annotated properties","text":"Clients MUST inspect inputSchema for x-mcp-header properties, encode values per Value Encoding, and append Mcp-Param-{Name} headers, omitting the header when no value is present."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t33o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t33c3","object":"call tools/list then retry","predicate":"SHOULD","stance":"reported","subject":"client response to HeaderMismatch","text":"On a HeaderMismatch rejection for missing or mismatched Mcp-Param-* headers, the client SHOULD call tools/list to check inputSchema changes, then retry with appropriate headers."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t33o5","t33o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t33c5","object":"HTTP 400 and error -32020 HeaderMismatch","predicate":"MUST be rejected with","stance":"reported","subject":"header-body validation failure","text":"Servers processing the body MUST validate decoded header values against body values and reject failures with HTTP 400 and JSON-RPC error -32020 (HeaderMismatch)."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t33o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t33c6","object":"case-insensitive (values case-sensitive)","predicate":"MUST be","stance":"reported","subject":"header name comparison","text":"Header names are case-insensitive and clients and servers MUST compare them case-insensitively, while header values such as method names are case-sensitive."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t33o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t33c8","object":"JSON-RPC error response","predicate":"MUST return HTTP error but need not return","stance":"qualified","subject":"intermediary validation failure responses","text":"Intermediaries MUST return an appropriate HTTP error status (e.g., 400) for validation failures but are not required to return a JSON-RPC error response."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t33o10"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t33c9","object":"requests with old or absent MCP-Protocol-Version","predicate":"SHOULD verify and SHOULD reject","stance":"qualified","subject":"intermediaries enforcing mirrored-header policy","text":"Intermediaries enforcing policy on mirrored headers SHOULD verify MCP-Protocol-Version requires header-body validation, and SHOULD reject requests when the version is older or the header absent."},{"based_on":["t33o3","t33o8","t33o10"],"falsifier":"A later revision stating these SHOULD items as unconditional MUST requirements without change, or a statement that they are final.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t33h1","text":"The section's optionality (client SHOULD retry after tools/list; server SHOULD compare integers numerically; intermediary SHOULD checks) is normative but soft and could be tightened to MUST in later revisions."},{"based_on":["t33o10","t33o7"],"falsifier":"A statement in the document mandating intermediary rejection of old or absent MCP-Protocol-Version, or evidence that validation occurs regardless.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t33h2","text":"Because intermediaries are only SHOULD-bound to verify MCP-Protocol-Version before trusting mirrored headers, header-body validation can be bypassed by older or headerless requests, leaving a security gap open."},{"about":["intermediary policy","MCP-Protocol-Version","header-body validation"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t33q1","needed":"Check later specification revisions of the transport/header validation section for strengthened intermediary requirements.","text":"Does any later revision make the intermediary MCP-Protocol-Version verification a MUST or otherwise close the unvalidated-header trust gap?"},{"about":["HeaderMismatch","x-mcp-header","error codes"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t33q2","needed":"Check the schema and error-code sections of this and later revisions for stability or experimental markers.","text":"Is the -32020 HeaderMismatch code and the x-mcp-header schema extension stable, or experimental and subject to change?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530"],"ranges":[["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530",20841,26565]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"4fec772407e