{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"f332ddfad6189c3974e7d6224dd175396847b0310006557f935d51f799cf2954","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"TR39-027452cf14b782b8","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"| Modern   | Legacy   | Fails. The server may reject the request with an implementation-defined error, stay silent, or even process an era-ambiguous method under legacy semantics.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t39_o1","terms":["modern client","legacy server","failure modes","implementation-defined error"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"On stdio, clients **SHOULD** send `server/discover` first to fail deterministically; the client then surfaces an actionable error to the user.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t39_o2","terms":["stdio","server/discover","SHOULD","deterministic failure"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"| Legacy   | Modern   | Fails. stdio: the server rejects `initialize` with a JSON-RPC error; the exact code is implementation-defined","kind":"observe","local_id":"t39_o3","terms":["legacy client","modern server","initialize rejection","implementation-defined code"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"Legacy clients have no fall-forward mechanism.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t39_o4","terms":["legacy clients","no fall-forward","interoperability limitation"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"A dual-era server **MAY** serve both eras concurrently on the same endpoint","kind":"observe","local_id":"t39_o5","terms":["dual-era server","MAY","concurrent eras"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"| Legacy   | Legacy   | Works according to the legacy revision; out of scope for this document.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t39_o6","terms":["legacy-legacy","out of scope"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"An `initialize` request selects legacy semantics, scoped to the stdio\n  process (stdio) or the session (HTTP), as specified by the negotiated\n  legacy protocol version.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t39_o7","terms":["initialize","legacy semantics","session scoping"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t39_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t39_c1","object":"implementation-defined (reject, silence, or legacy-semantics processing)","predicate":"fails with behavior that is","stance":"reported","subject":"modern client with legacy server","text":"A modern client against a legacy server fails, but the server's behavior is implementation-defined: it may reject, stay silent, or process an era-ambiguous method under legacy semantics."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t39_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t39_c2","object":"server/discover to fail deterministically","predicate":"SHOULD send first","stance":"qualified","subject":"stdio clients against legacy servers","text":"On stdio, clients SHOULD send server/discover first when facing a legacy server so failure is deterministic, then surface an actionable error to the user."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t39_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t39_c3","object":"implementation-defined JSON-RPC error on initialize (stdio)","predicate":"fails with","stance":"reported","subject":"legacy client with modern server","text":"A legacy client against a modern server fails; on stdio the server rejects initialize with a JSON-RPC error whose exact code is implementation-defined."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t39_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t39_c4","object":"any fall-forward mechanism","predicate":"lack","stance":"reported","subject":"legacy clients","text":"Legacy clients have no fall-forward mechanism, so legacy-to-modern interoperability failure is unrecoverable from the client side."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t39_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t39_c5","object":"both eras on the same endpoint or process","predicate":"MAY serve concurrently","stance":"qualified","subject":"dual-era server","text":"A dual-era server MAY serve both eras concurrently on the same endpoint or process; concurrent dual-era service is optional, not required."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t39_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t39_c6","object":"out of scope for this document","predicate":"is","stance":"reported","subject":"legacy client with legacy server","text":"Legacy-to-legacy operation works per the legacy revision but is explicitly out of scope for this document."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t39_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t39_c7","object":"modern _meta vs initialize request","predicate":"is determined by","stance":"reported","subject":"dual-era server era selection","text":"A dual-era server selects era from the opening request: modern per-request _meta is served statelessly, while initialize selects legacy semantics scoped to the stdio process or HTTP session."},{"based_on":["t39_o1","t39_o2"],"falsifier":"A later revision making the stdio server/discover probe a MUST, or specifying the legacy server's rejection behavior as normative rather than implementation-defined.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t39_h1","text":"The compatibility matrix leaves the modern-client/legacy-server failure mode open: because the server may stay silent or process era-ambiguous methods under legacy semantics, deterministic detection depends on the SHOULD-level server/discover probe, which a later revision could tighten to MUST."},{"based_on":["t39_o3","t39_o4"],"falsifier":"A later revision adding a fall-forward or upgrade mechanism for legacy clients, or declaring legacy client support deprecated/removed.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t39_h2","text":"Legacy clients' lack of any fall-forward mechanism is an acknowledged interoperability limitation that remains open for future work, since the matrix offers no recovery path for legacy-to-modern failures."},{"about":["implementation-defined errors","compatibility matrix"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t39_q1","needed":"Check later revisions of the compatibility section for normative error codes replacing 'implementation-defined'.","text":"Is the implementation-defined error behavior for modern-client/legacy-server and legacy-client/modern-server combinations later pinned down normatively?"},{"about":["dual-era server","MAY concurrency"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t39_q2","needed":"Check subsequent revision of this section for change in modality of the dual-era concurrency statement.","text":"Does any later revision make concurrent dual-era service (currently MAY) a requirement or remove it?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa"],"ranges":[["d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa",5784,11293]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"0d465874c5aba70742e837a4d723aa15c4265da2979060de75c09e8dae4814fa","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["345e52cf86c489938fb4a0eb047764559469762f03d27796cbf4af12fa60f6f8","2e2b98c236