ecification; the conformance level is a SHOULD, not a MUST."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t35_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t35_c3","object":"this specification","predicate":"SHOULD NOT follow","stance":"reported","subject":"STDIO transport implementations","text":"STDIO implementations SHOULD NOT follow this specification and instead retrieve credentials from the environment, which limits the scope of the HTTP authorization rules."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t35_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t35_c5","object":"IETF draft draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13 with selected subset","predicate":"is","stance":"open","subject":"OAuth 2.1 basis","text":"The spec's OAuth 2.1 basis is an IETF draft (draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13) and implements only a selected subset of referenced features; the section does not state whether the draft is finalized."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t35_o9","t35_o10"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t35_c7","object":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document-00","predicate":"SHOULD be supported; pinned to","stance":"open","subject":"Client ID Metadata Documents","text":"Client ID Metadata Documents support is a SHOULD for authorization servers and clients; the section pins the reference to draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document-00."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t35_o13","t35_o14"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t35_c8","object":"OAuth 2.0 Protected Resource Metadata (RFC9728)","predicate":"MUST implement and use","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP servers and clients","text":"MCP servers MUST implement RFC9728 Protected Resource Metadata, and MCP clients MUST use it for authorization server discovery."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d"],"ranges":[["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d",0,5816]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"e22e8abebee861b54fc0389dff0952e133cea9a3817bdeaacc6fcdd40089c5e0","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["c2a2dfb80e46363adc06b3a778766c5fe7503e4f