{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"5f4314290369b0a56b77d771fde4c368b06feb13432439f0e88c3c79eff86d30","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"TR40-a8de8e92405bb199","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"Authorization is **OPTIONAL** for MCP implementations. When supported:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t40_o1","terms":["authorization optionality","protocol requirements"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"OAuth 2.1 IETF DRAFT ([draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13))","kind":"observe","local_id":"t40_o3","terms":["OAuth 2.1 draft dependency","standards compliance"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"Authorization servers and MCP clients **SHOULD** support [OAuth Client ID Metadata Documents]","kind":"observe","local_id":"t40_o5","terms":["Client ID Metadata Documents","SHOULD support"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"is deprecated and retained for backwards compatibility with authorization servers that do not support Client ID Metadata Documents.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t40_o6","terms":["Dynamic Client Registration deprecation","backwards compatibility"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"MCP servers **MUST** implement OAuth 2.0 Protected Resource Metadata ([RFC9728](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9728)).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t40_o7","terms":["Protected Resource Metadata","MUST implement"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"MCP clients **MUST** support both [discovery mechanisms](/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/authorization-server-discovery#authorization-server-metadata-discovery)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t40_o8","terms":["discovery mechanisms","client MUST support both"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"Before initiating the authorization flow, MCP clients **MUST** obtain a client ID through","kind":"observe","local_id":"t40_o9","terms":["client registration","client ID acquisition"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t40_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t40_c1","object":"MCP implementations; this specification","predicate":"is OPTIONAL for; HTTP transports SHOULD conform to","stance":"reported","subject":"authorization support","text":"Authorization is OPTIONAL for MCP implementations; when supported, HTTP-based transports SHOULD conform to this specification."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t40_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t40_c3","object":"OAuth 2.1 IETF DRAFT draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13","predicate":"is based on","stance":"reported","subject":"authorization mechanism basis","text":"The authorization mechanism is based on OAuth 2.1 IETF DRAFT draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13, a draft rather than a final RFC."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t40_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t40_c5","object":"authorization servers and MCP clients","predicate":"SHOULD be supported by","stance":"reported","subject":"OAuth Client ID Metadata Documents","text":"Authorization servers and MCP clients SHOULD support OAuth Client ID Metadata Documents (draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document-00)."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t40_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t40_c7","object":"authorization server discovery","predicate":"MUST be implemented by servers and used by clients for","stance":"reported","subject":"OAuth 2.0 Protected Resource Metadata","text":"MCP servers MUST implement OAuth 2.0 Protected Resource Metadata (RFC9728), and MCP clients MUST use it for authorization server discovery."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t40_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t40_c8","object":"RFC8414 metadata and OpenID Connect Discovery","predicate":"MUST provide at least one of; clients MUST support both","stance":"reported","subject":"authorization server discovery mechanisms","text":"MCP authorization servers MUST provide at least one of RFC8414 metadata or OpenID Connect Discovery, and MCP clients MUST support both discovery mechanisms."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t40_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t40_c9","object":"Client ID Metadata Documents, pre-registration, or Dynamic Client Registration","predicate":"MUST occur before authorization flow via","stance":"reported","subject":"client ID acquisition","text":"Before initiating the authorization flow, MCP clients MUST obtain a client ID via Client ID Metadata Documents, pre-registration, or Dynamic Client Registration."},{"based_on":["t40_o3"],"falsifier":"A statement in the document pinning draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13 as stable, or a later revision adopting the final RFC without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t40_h1","text":"The OAuth 2.1 requirements here are provisional because they rest on an IETF draft (draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13) and may be qualified once finalized."},{"based_on":["t40_o5","t40_o6"],"falsifier":"A later revision stating Client ID Metadata Documents support as MUST or removing the deprecation of Dynamic Client Registration without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t40_h2","text":"Client ID Metadata Documents support (SHOULD) and deprecated Dynamic Client Registration (MAY) are the section's main open registration items likely to be tightened or qualified later."},{"about":["OAuth 2.1 draft dependency","provisional requirements"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t40_q1","needed":"Check later revisions of the Authorization section for the cited OAuth 2.1 reference and any changed normative language.","text":"Does a later revision replace draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13 with a final OAuth 2.1 RFC, and if so which requirements change?"},{"about":["client registration","deprecation status"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t40_q2","needed":"Compare the Client Registration and Overview requirements in later revisions of this section.","text":"Do later revisions tighten Client ID Metadata Documents from SHOULD to MUST or drop the Dynamic Client Registration deprecation?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d"],"ranges":[["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d",0,5816]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"fa2f9ab6f356b1109c6045c00cd6d35205ba1cb0ffcdf422b03712576aeea25f","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["be6e810b091c3b871a026d3d3979c570c1d4273cb6d5cb7e56f6dc198cded4d4","c5f5f982b87114054000774e35de1da1959f60a650bbc15e05a3cda4e495effa","a3d2d73b725f80d987e4944d6091698d0844f165034fb3365ad25f7561697771","c39781e5ffb7de9d4c499d4dd3f26085c5393dcd55f7abcf76cd4921f34be6e2","04d30bd19a516f6e740dc4d2bf727a799621b1a5927e16291ba642ea02079349","ae648c58f07491793e66628de31da360ab5f49c50e6961b069e323affe6bae88","304ee2a90434a2e6f942f793d59172d227dfdcc3fd9be8c726e782f226d2309d","7a046d15cad74e70c9c6b96c4aa7696e01c27d4a2806ad57337d59875000c61c","327fd04fa287f0350b4b90e882146bc85aa7706f65da83d7bac70fb40291e923","2928063e08024190edebfebffd618850