{"body":{"actor":"w2","audit_root":"bc63f42bbb52cbba0048e6a98702c636a889371099965b58aa1fbdf03f3c2669","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"TR41-6364894ba7058df3","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"**Modern**: protocol versions that convey version, identity, and\n  capabilities as per-request metadata (revision `2026-07-28` and later).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t41_o3","terms":["definition of modern protocol versions"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"**Legacy**: protocol versions that establish a session with an\n  `initialize` handshake (`2025-11-25` and earlier).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t41_o5","terms":["definition of legacy protocol versions with initialize handshake"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"If the server does not implement the requested version (whether the version\nis unknown to the server, or is a known version the server has chosen not to\nsupport), it **MUST** respond with an\n[`UnsupportedProtocolVersionError`](/specification/2026-07-28/schema#unsupportedprotocolversionerror)\nlisting the versions it does support:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t41_o6","terms":["server must answer unsupported version with UnsupportedProtocolVersionError listing supported versions"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"If one party supports an extension but the other does not, the supporting\nparty **MUST** either revert to core protocol behavior or reject the request","kind":"observe","local_id":"t41_o11","terms":["fallback when only one party supports an extension"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"probe with `server/discover` and fall back on any error that is not a\n  recognized modern error.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t41_o13","terms":["stdio era detection by probing"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"process (stdio) or origin (HTTP), and **MAY** persist it across restarts of\nthe same server configuration, re-probing if the cached assumption later\nfails.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t41_o16","terms":["persisting era cache across restarts with re-probe on failure"]},{"as_of":20260728,"based_on":["@9b58f70763501ac1","@87e822c21b11289b","t41_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t41_c1","object":"per-request version declaration in _meta","predicate":"has no handshake; each request is accepted or rejected independently","stance":"qualified","subject":"version negotiation for modern protocol versions","text":"Modern protocol versions have no negotiation handshake; each request declares its version and the server accepts or rejects it independently. The initialize handshake remains for legacy versions."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t41_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t41_c2","object":"UnsupportedProtocolVersionError listing supported versions","predicate":"MUST respond with","stance":"reported","subject":"server receiving an unsupported protocol version","text":"A server that does not implement the requested protocol version MUST respond with UnsupportedProtocolVersionError listing the versions it does support."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t41_o6","@44504df799b2f46a"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t41_c3","object":"version from the supported list","predicate":"SHOULD select and retry a mutually supported version","stance":"reported","subject":"client receiving UnsupportedProtocolVersionError","text":"On UnsupportedProtocolVersionError the client SHOULD select a mutually supported version from the supported list and retry, or surface an error if none exists."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t41_o11"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t41_c6","object":"core protocol behavior or appropriate error","predicate":"MUST revert to core behavior or reject the request","stance":"reported","subject":"supporting party when the other party lacks an extension","text":"If only one party supports an extension, the supporting party MUST either revert to core protocol behavior or reject the request with an appropriate error."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t41_o13","@d88c90cbd08023f6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t41_c8","object":"server/discover probe on stdio; modern request and 400 body inspection on Streamable HTTP","predicate":"is performed by","stance":"reported","subject":"client era detection","text":"Clients detect server era by probing with server/discover over stdio (falling back on non-modern errors) and, over Streamable HTTP, by attempting a modern request and inspecting a 400 Bad Request body."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@48c3c998052f6efc","t41_o16"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t41_c9","object":"server process lifetime or origin","predicate":"SHOULD be cached; MAY be persisted; re-probed on failure","stance":"reported","subject":"era determination cache","text":"Clients SHOULD cache the era determination for the lifetime of the server process (stdio) or origin (HTTP), MAY persist it across restarts, and re-probe if the cached assumption fails."},{"based_on":["t41_o16","@a8e1d62ba9c873f4","@48c3c998052f6efc"],"falsifier":"A later revision of this section specifying cache invalidation or a required re-probe on server upgrade without relying on the existing failure-triggered re-probe.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t41_h1","text":"Persisted era determinations may become stale when a server is upgraded to modern-only or dual-era, so clients relying on the cache depend on the re-probe rule to avoid wrong fallbacks."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa"],"ranges":[["d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa",0,5784]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"cc71c0802e9c57b11f57e39177ac2cad5c45c3c4991ffd127e7a0f387eb38111","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["5bef6b8856390b21e70e4c5de5cf4ba419d90be5fe72371867663309999a941f","b8752850c9a052e5b8aabd01325e01458729eab988637b230e259c524db034a8","4ece666519ce08b91d3a3d44883c1faeb2555bed7d81d4529bfe4dccd8e84ac6","fbb9fdc8308c050e01dccd08367573c79c5d88af5f5eeeb569e631df53cd53bf","412c1ecc0e87d52c5d75e3c455b12864cb59cdaaf9af4c7ec2542a2f42ecdd8a","8516f433ed5d9a2ac80b31d63ae63f5aadfb07b531acc75e007d82e5647175b7","ca4aec9353152fc5c7db2cd7f9f784d4b4ba95594ccda2162eb26b5a4305fbfb","72b303ae2ba9e1ca4ce20b331f41a5905c341273f285ee43d6daf58def000a84","6bef3aa91047ae382cc128f8195d37be8eed2657e4feb51a0d1b538a98390e0b","d02f144e053f8f67a391bb46947a5bf3a823bb50de4011b755b6da3f404c7aa3","1e20a0431636f3ffebd19d1f9c9f4660c06a3236dadd9c6958fcb43ef2903820","8b289f3269fb959aa3e81ee51716d1f97e99b567c01178e37627b5491f3c3e72","88ef115b0f5ce1ee1146fefd15aa14db710a639b822965fb5d58c3d794031fdd"],"error":null,"failed_index":null}},"request_hash":"0955a75d64f69f89c2116ab5912ad04b40c088c393da9d9535f15ae0a25f0107","submission_id":"TR41-6364894ba7058df3#2"},"hash":"5cca93c2b0b23cd23159d901f62ca93823e3003f5f03e9cf8f942d76d146ee5d","header":{"body_hash":"11904ef191ceef1ea9660bbd6592c7dc1e58265c2989a1d8