{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"44e374e1ff0b142a05805f58d471077bd9a551e17153ca852d6db519f49dab51","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T45-9428a866ccee2d7b","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"A future revision of this specification is expected to upgrade authorization server inclusion of `iss` from **SHOULD** to **MUST**.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t45_o1","terms":["iss parameter","future revision","SHOULD to MUST"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"client rejection behavior on `iss` absence will continue to be keyed on `authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported` until that revision defines the upgrade path.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t45_o2","terms":["iss absence","rejection behavior","upgrade path open"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"MCP authorization servers **SHOULD** include the `iss` parameter in authorization responses, including error responses","kind":"observe","local_id":"t45_o3","terms":["iss parameter","authorization servers","SHOULD"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"The validation in this section depends on that recorded value being authentic; it provides no protection if the expected issuer was obtained from an unvalidated source.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t45_o4","terms":["issuer validation","limitation","unvalidated source"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"this specification compares a present `iss` against the recorded issuer regardless of metadata advertisement","kind":"observe","local_id":"t45_o5","terms":["local-policy provision","iss comparison","metadata advertisement"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"MCP clients **MUST** implement Resource Indicators for OAuth 2.0 as defined in [RFC 8707]","kind":"observe","local_id":"t45_o6","terms":["Resource Indicators","RFC 8707","MUST"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t45_o1","t45_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t45_c1","object":"a future revision of this specification","predicate":"is expected to be upgraded from SHOULD to MUST in","stance":"open","subject":"authorization server inclusion of iss parameter","text":"Authorization server inclusion of the iss parameter is currently SHOULD, with a future revision expected to upgrade it to MUST; implementers are encouraged to emit and validate iss now."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t45_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t45_c2","object":"that revision defines the upgrade path","predicate":"will continue to be keyed on authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported until","stance":"open","subject":"client rejection behavior on iss absence","text":"Client rejection behavior on iss absence remains keyed on authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported until a future revision defines the upgrade path, leaving that behavior open."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t45_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t45_c3","object":"the expected issuer was obtained from an unvalidated source","predicate":"provides no protection if","stance":"reported","subject":"issuer validation in this section","text":"Issuer validation provides no protection if the expected issuer was obtained from an unvalidated source, a stated limitation of this section."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t45_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t45_c4","object":"Resource Indicators for OAuth 2.0 as defined in RFC 8707","predicate":"MUST implement","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP clients","text":"MCP clients MUST implement Resource Indicators for OAuth 2.0 per RFC 8707, with the resource parameter required in both authorization and token requests."},{"based_on":["t45_o1","t45_o2","t45_o3"],"falsifier":"A later revision leaving iss inclusion at SHOULD and the rejection behavior unchanged, or a statement that no upgrade is planned.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t45_h1","text":"The SHOULD-level iss inclusion and the undefined upgrade path for iss-absence rejection are the section's main items likely to be tightened in a later revision."},{"about":["iss parameter","future revision","upgrade path"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t45_q1","needed":"Check later revisions of the authorization response validation section for the promised SHOULD-to-MUST upgrade and upgrade-path definition.","text":"Does a later revision of this specification upgrade iss inclusion from SHOULD to MUST and define the iss-absence rejection upgrade path?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d"],"ranges":[["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d",10530,14820]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"a4e3f23ad39b82706e44f885cb5956630c00f0e07721485cc6757822e8c41d54","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["34e4314f4745144a1c0110dd8b0435daf5b90b2ceb6003a68298d8d607f35c71","27ca2c04ba282fdb97aaf0725bb78f30922290208d519759c6dc9b22adda5800","8e9a28b0a2ba19b1bd016a8cebac2af82b1c98b848bfb3ab481bd50aa9774344",