ed","subject":"access token handling conformance","text":"Access token handling MUST conform to OAuth 2.1 draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13 Section 5, so conformance is pinned to a draft revision rather than a final RFC."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t46_o12","t46_o13"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t46_c7","object":"refresh tokens / offline_access","predicate":"MUST NOT be assumed and SHOULD NOT be advertised as resource requirement","stance":"qualified","subject":"refresh token issuance","text":"Clients MUST NOT assume refresh tokens will be issued since the authorization server retains discretion; servers SHOULD NOT advertise offline_access as a resource requirement."},{"based_on":["t46_o5"],"falsifier":"A statement in the document pinning the draft as stable, or a later revision citing the final RFC without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t46_h1","text":"The section's OAuth 2.1 obligations are pinned to draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13/-14, so they may be qualified once the draft is finalized as an RFC."},{"based_on":["t46_o2","t46_o3","t46_o4","t46_o13"],"falsifier":"A later revision stating these SHOULD/SHOULD NOT items as unconditional MUST requirements without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t46_h2","text":"Canonical URI and refresh-token rules are normative but leave SHOULD/SHOULD NOT optionality that later revisions could tighten to MUST."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d"],"ranges":[["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d",14820,20184]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"9e1b9f54b7b97a64d030332dd2070c5a1d9f32dbd3c1d1b288e3206f0839bd01","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["946ad9363e0fe704081be6b8e041871890d5c5e2ea70faabe419bebbe33d2ddd","9c39e9c319ed7361b25d6b4db54168776169c878b8516e3c9c0c4e45ae878164","f75a8b2c0643abfee19692b198c2e010103b8b0cac4b45f9a2dfc8ade48b67ce","5a709bcaddd64ea252fc06863c8281705f1ea380e6350de1ecac3d169f5d10d5","a0bd9adf617b92c6a357e2d9532acab0f