{"body":{"actor":"w4","audit_root":"ca9f4d11823aadc87cc5de89ed1f92d859dc154e3fe3d5a456db64fa3abd55d6","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T42-696ec9d7434c1344","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"The scopes included in the `WWW-Authenticate` challenge **MAY** match `scopes_supported`, be a subset","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o2","terms":["WWW-Authenticate challenge","scopes_supported","scope relationship"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"superset. Clients **MUST NOT** assume any particular set relationship between the challenged\nscope set and `scopes_supported`.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o3","terms":["challenged scope set","scopes_supported","client assumption"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t42_o2","t42_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t42_c2","object":"clients","predicate":"MUST NOT be assumed by","stance":"reported","subject":"set relationship between challenged scopes and scopes_supported","text":"Challenged scopes may match, subset, superset, or differ from scopes_supported, and clients MUST NOT assume any set relationship between them."},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"consistency in how they construct scope sets but they are not required to surface every dynamically\nissued scope through `scopes_supported`.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o5","terms":["scope sets","dynamically issued scope","scopes_supported"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t42_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t42_c4","object":"scopes_supported","predicate":"are not required to be surfaced in","stance":"qualified","subject":"dynamically issued scopes","text":"Servers are not required to expose every dynamically issued scope in scopes_supported, qualifying the completeness of scopes_supported."},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"When re-authorizing, clients **SHOULD** include these scopes\nalongside any previously granted scopes to avoid losing permissions needed for other operations","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o6","terms":["re-authorizing","granted scopes","clients"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t42_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t42_c5","object":"clients","predicate":"SHOULD be included alongside challenged scopes when re-authorizing by","stance":"qualified","subject":"previously granted scopes","text":"Clients SHOULD retain previously granted scopes alongside challenged scopes when re-authorizing to avoid losing permissions."},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"**SHOULD** follow this priority order for scope selection:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o7","terms":["scope selection","priority order","MCP clients"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"1. **Use `scope` parameter** from the initial `WWW-Authenticate` header in the 401 response, if provided","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o8","terms":["scope parameter priority","WWW-Authenticate header","401 response"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"2. **If `scope` is not available**, use all scopes defined in `scopes_supported` from the Protected Resource Metadata document, omitting the `scope` parameter if `scopes_supported` is undefined.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o9","terms":["fallback scope selection","scopes_supported","Protected Resource Metadata"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t42_o7","t42_o8","t42_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t42_c6","object":"MCP clients","predicate":"SHOULD be followed by","stance":"qualified","subject":"scope selection priority order","text":"Initial scope selection priority order (first 401 scope parameter if provided, else all scopes_supported, else omit) is a SHOULD recommendation."},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"The registration step shown in the flow uses one of the mechanisms defined in\n[Client Registration](/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/client-registration).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o10","terms":["client registration mechanisms","authorization flow","specification link"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"    alt Client ID Metadata Documents","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o11","terms":["Client ID Metadata Documents","client registration alternative"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"    else Dynamic client registration","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o12","terms":["Dynamic client registration","client registration alternative"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"    else Pre-registered client","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o13","terms":["Pre-registered client","client registration alternative"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t42_o10","t42_o11","t42_o12","t42_o13"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t42_c7","object":"Client ID Metadata Documents, dynamic registration, or pre-registration","predicate":"supports alternatives of","stance":"reported","subject":"client registration in authorization flow","text":"Client registration accommodates three alternative mechanisms: Client ID Metadata Documents, Dynamic client registration, and Pre-registered client."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t42_o11","t42_o12","t42_o13"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t42_c8","object":"dynamic and pre-registered client mechanisms","predicate":"is specified as an alternative alongside","stance":"qualified","subject":"Client ID Metadata Documents registration","text":"Client ID Metadata Documents is not mandated as the exclusive registration mechanism, refuting any requirement of exclusivity."},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"    Note over C: Parse metadata and extract authorization server(s)<br/>Client determines AS to use","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o14","terms":["authorization server selection","client determination"]},{"doc_id":"d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d","exact_quote":"    Note over C,A: Try OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect<br/>discovery endpoints in priority order","kind":"observe","local_id":"t42_o15","terms":["discovery endpoints priority","OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t42_o14","t42_o15"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t42_c9","object":"client trying OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect discovery endpoints","predicate":"is determined by","stance":"reported","subject":"authorization server discovery and selection","text":"Client determines which authorization server to use and tries OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect discovery endpoints in priority order."},{"about":["OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect discovery priority","authorization server metadata"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t42_q1","needed":"Check discovery specifications or step-up authorization flow section for conflict resolution rules.","text":"How are priority order conflicts resolved if both OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect discovery endpoints are advertised and return conflicting metadata?"},{"based_on":["t42_o10","t42_o11"],"falsifier":"A subsequent specification revision designating Client ID Metadata Documents as the mandatory sole registration mechanism.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t42_h1","text":"Client ID Metadata Documents registration remains optional across future revisions rather than being made an unconditional MUST."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d"],"ranges":[["d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c88d2ff29d",5816,10530]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"9f7378c73afa8e4f09f978bfc839a462a0404a33228a6fa55917becfef41f972","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["dd4e330b6e3c7b98cd27030aff8d2097dd717c0eae0fe6008ea0ae88ceaf7510","2cb222c00543ac7abf8d2866e3c1c298c0af52e62d013610b3f173660e002286","11b3788460067b82dc9c18c7a58ea48ba76423f224af87f64e4f919539f333eb","59c64460331d4b03619da6fa671bb8fa6e26e529133834ceac5682942ec20fc5","b9fcef37291799c1c4f100bf76375685bb9576b6819f5a13dc258a4cf12695f9","d8110c1e45b4898fb224f9459494daeb1ba011013f50c8cea385f619de65a75d","5694a9812937741d2abc1c50641ef39b532b2963fba5abbbeb202699645b99ee","9c88c6250e92a57fd2bea1dfc411d87d78c2fb2dfee4ea2f39986263ac79267c","9d2bbc9f00df03a59e9873db9e1ed43fb92e198dba1a8b41a1abb68343af5320","451617a75f652072d11a3173940bf53836104c642d3ed293aad2c07e5134def1","63368db4f00ce00a7a07825ffb2fcc20f16e3830d1b396a2eff79e545d7aa410","dc1a2596c0fa445036779d9f325d32558ddadb8dbb8d3af97fb8103fcca1a9e4","ac225c0e602f6fa05c4b7c311a78c1f7d404be0afb35882baab93289ef979a21","cdd5ca46f6216fedf9f2260c4a4283d50bce5e1b6d89f6514f4c4fea31134bf5","0d184fa77db4882fe05f41069b1c36701e1afb6459c2d46a822c72f0ec3c77f2","114a9c0b70a49ee47148c343e5772d63ea472a272473cba435820524e9220869","408eb9a1cdae65725c74bb542cfa7cb8074d68006af4ce374647c0d2cec68c23","a29a1d7fd