{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"a59830f3703c8465b9fd93f57ad991882d6ab7b51c91aa92bc58a88fa4f2f70c","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"TR59-5695de4ea44b318c","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"All implementations **MUST** support the base protocol, versioning,","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o1","terms":["mandatory components","base protocol","versioning","message patterns"]},{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"- Unlike base JSON-RPC, the ID **MUST NOT** be `null`.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o4","terms":["request ID","null prohibition","deviation from JSON-RPC"]},{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"- The `result` **MUST** include a `resultType` field to indicate the type of the result.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o6","terms":["resultType","result response requirement"]},{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"- A `resultType` of `\"input_required\"` indicates the request is incomplete and more information is needed to process the request.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o7","terms":["input_required","multi round-trip requests","MRTR"]},{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"- Extensions **MAY** add additional `ResultType` values.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o8","terms":["extensions","ResultType extensibility","MAY"]},{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"- A `resultType` of any value unrecognized by the client **MUST** be considered invalid.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o9","terms":["unrecognized resultType","invalid result"]},{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"- For backward compatibility with servers implementing earlier protocol versions, which do not include `resultType`, clients **MUST** treat an absent `resultType` as `\"complete\"`.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o10","terms":["backward compatibility","absent resultType","earlier protocol versions"]},{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"- Error responses **MUST** include the same ID as the request they correspond to (except in error cases where the ID could not be read due a malformed request).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o11","terms":["error response ID","malformed request exception"]},{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","exact_quote":"- Error responses **MAY** include a `data` member with additional information of any type, such","kind":"observe","local_id":"t59_o12","terms":["error data member","MAY"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t59_o6","t59_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t59_c4","object":"incomplete request needing more information","predicate":"MUST be included in result responses, with input_required meaning","stance":"reported","subject":"resultType field","text":"Result responses MUST include a resultType field; a resultType of \"input_required\" signals the request is incomplete and more information is needed."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t59_o8","t59_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t59_c5","object":"invalid","predicate":"MAY be added, while unrecognized values MUST be treated as","stance":"reported","subject":"extension-defined ResultType values","text":"Extensions MAY add ResultType values, but a resultType unrecognized by the client MUST be considered invalid."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t59_o10"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t59_c6","object":"\"complete\"","predicate":"MUST be treated as","stance":"reported","subject":"absent resultType from earlier-version servers","text":"For backward compatibility with earlier protocol versions lacking resultType, clients MUST treat an absent resultType as \"complete\"."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t59_o11","t59_o12"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t59_c7","object":"data member","predicate":"MUST include matching ID (with malformed-request exception) and MAY include","stance":"reported","subject":"error responses","text":"Error responses MUST include the request's ID except where the ID could not be read due to a malformed request, and MAY include a data member."},{"based_on":["t59_o10","t59_o6"],"falsifier":"A statement in this section or a cited earlier revision showing resultType existed in earlier protocol versions.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t59_h1","text":"The resultType field and its backward-compatibility rule (absent treated as \"complete\") are new in this revision, so earlier-version servers are implicitly qualified as non-conforming to the resultType requirement."},{"based_on":["t59_o8","t59_o9"],"falsifier":"Text stating clients must accept extension ResultType values regardless of advertised capabilities.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t59_h2","text":"Because extensions MAY add ResultType values while unrecognized values MUST be invalid, extension-defined result types are an open interoperability risk for clients not advertising the extension."},{"about":["t59_c4","t59_c5"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t59_q1","needed":"Check versioning/compatibility section and changelog for resultType introduction and any MUST tightening.","text":"Does the section date or version-stamp the resultType requirement, and does any later revision tighten the MAY for extension ResultType values?"},{"about":["t59_c7"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t59_q2","needed":"Check error-handling or schema sections for malformed request ID guidance.","text":"Is the malformed-request exception to the error-response ID rule further specified elsewhere (e.g., what ID to use)?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb"],"ranges":[["d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb",0,4563]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"4a0da32185a525acef34e020915bb8316fad03c6582fb626aa78847f50ea2bc5","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["2cda662d7de22fc6cadb384773eecab1e8d84c210b33c54c49301a838561ae1a","a086a10a89119293569ed55083e7fd5ed57537114fe1af0cbfe026ab61b7a5ec","bc84f78ab74286960f31b0c0d5a103cf4c980a496daf3c1719259ea5eee2f46b","6ffea1289e3d256ed33a3d7620825321297c7efcef13106b96b0b7116f911e18","47d836acc85d3506ae9fd8c58ec7fbc2bba13309ef51ae49cf97a99df32b9c7c","a75fa09ba0a45d2a108c2be93368a108398fbff336ed2b94c69833b8160b4ab2","4c1381c9d36c24b5e7b9d72830ec87e92a2f33daae34795cfc317effcc1e8312","30a07ea43173fa2e7223f72ae1b96bfbdcfcd880201e7ff9f179c4f48e3ec3b9","1441bbaaf7c85b912b93c8901d1fc172749ef3f90a694a90f527b509cddfdd54","363120ca34ce20e07c820cbb61fdc1d9a5b93b54e0fe45c5bcd098c3ad40bd10","f1ccb7413246e0bf01d67fabca3991abc05246b4533acd589ab3327947bf1ab5","52f58b1153599df4142bcc1f04bcaa8aadac42532473e1acd1a4077aceb36a95","82ba6a48f7882910d5e48bbab1811e38c17f3152e053c590e8eecb24b8b5bf99","2e0468ea1fddbdc678b402485e2db5bee43bd3505846549cfbba877074784c76","517c9997705d0a0c984ff6a3c537fdea44c1bd689f6e6a7b59834ae66fb13d73","a74bc53a9de7e5dd9fe2834246cf7d