{"body":{"actor":"w2","audit_root":"7767cdcf720fb7798c4170f77e9339edfcfe66021791f1f976be10a6230f4514","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T56-eeff61a849775e7a","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"The protocol currently defines two standard transport mechanisms for client-server","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o1","terms":["two standard transports","time-bound wording via 'currently'"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Servers **MUST** validate the `Origin` header on all incoming connections to prevent DNS rebinding attacks","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o2","terms":["Origin header validation","DNS rebinding protection"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Servers **SHOULD** implement proper authentication for all connections","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o3","terms":["server authentication strength","SHOULD rather than MUST"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Disconnection **SHOULD NOT** be interpreted as the client cancelling its request.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o4","terms":["disconnection is not cancellation"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"To cancel, the client **SHOULD** explicitly send an MCP `CancelledNotification`.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o5","terms":["explicit cancellation via CancelledNotification"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"[batch](https://www.jsonrpc.org/specification#batch) containing one or more requests","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o6","terms":["JSON-RPC batch in stdio messages"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"To avoid message loss due to disconnection, the server **MAY** make the stream","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o7","terms":["optional resumability of SSE stream"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"It is also possible for clients and servers to implement","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o9","terms":["custom transports are pluggable, defined elsewhere"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"This transport uses HTTP POST and GET requests.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o11","terms":["Streamable HTTP uses POST and GET"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Without these protections, attackers could use DNS rebinding to interact with local MCP servers from remote websites.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o12","terms":["rationale for security protections"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"The server **MAY** write UTF-8 strings to its standard error","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o15","terms":["stderr logging is optional"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"The SSE stream **SHOULD** eventually include one JSON-RPC _response_ per each","kind":"observe","local_id":"t56_o17","terms":["SSE stream should return responses for each request"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c1","object":"proper authentication for all connections","predicate":"SHOULD implement","stance":"qualified","subject":"server authentication for Streamable HTTP connections","text":"Server authentication on Streamable HTTP is only a SHOULD ('proper authentication for all connections'), not a MUST, so it is a qualified recommendation."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o2","t56_o12"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c2","object":"on all incoming connections","predicate":"MUST validate","stance":"reported","subject":"Origin header validation","text":"Servers MUST validate the Origin header on all incoming connections to prevent DNS rebinding attacks; the section gives the rationale for this protection."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c3","object":"two (stdio and Streamable HTTP)","predicate":"currently defines","stance":"reported","subject":"standard transport mechanisms","text":"The protocol currently defines two standard transports: stdio and Streamable HTTP. 'Currently' ties this to the present revision, so it may change."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c5","object":"the client cancelling its request","predicate":"SHOULD NOT be interpreted as","stance":"reported","subject":"client disconnection","text":"Client disconnection must not be read as a cancellation request, so cancellation requires an explicit notification."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c6","object":"MCP CancelledNotification","predicate":"SHOULD explicitly send","stance":"qualified","subject":"request cancellation","text":"To cancel a request, the client SHOULD explicitly send an MCP CancelledNotification; this is a recommendation, not a MUST."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c7","object":"resumable","predicate":"MAY be made","stance":"qualified","subject":"SSE stream resumability","text":"Stream resumability for avoiding message loss on disconnection is optional (MAY), and the referenced resumability mechanism is not defined in this section."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o17"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c9","object":"one JSON-RPC response per request","predicate":"SHOULD eventually include","stance":"qualified","subject":"SSE stream responses","text":"The server SHOULD eventually include one JSON-RPC response per request in the SSE stream; this is a SHOULD, not a MUST."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c10","object":"clients and servers","predicate":"is possible via pluggable implementation","stance":"open","subject":"custom transports","text":"Custom transports are possible through a pluggable mechanism, but this section does not specify them."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t56_o15"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t56_c13","object":"UTF-8 strings to stderr","predicate":"MAY be written","stance":"reported","subject":"stderr logging","text":"Servers MAY write UTF-8 logs to stderr and clients MAY capture, forward or ignore them; this logging is optional."},{"based_on":["t56_o3"],"falsifier":"A later revision of this transports section stating server authentication for all connections as a MUST without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t56_h1","text":"The SHOULD-level authentication requirement for Streamable HTTP servers may be tightened to MUST in a later revision, since the section leaves it optional."},{"about":["session management","resumability","custom transports"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t56_q1","needed":"Check the linked sections #session-management, #resumability-and-redelivery and #custom-transports in the same specification revision.","text":"Where are session management, resumability-and-redelivery and custom transports specified, and do they change the optional behaviour stated in this section?"},{"about":["JSON-RPC batching","transports"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t56_q2","needed":"Compare batching wording in the stdio and Streamable HTTP POST rules across the revisions that define this section.","text":"Does the revision that removed JSON-RPC batching (@8599201b) also remove the batch arrays still described in this transports section?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b"],"ranges":[["d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b",0,5820]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"ade10c2303c87733064effadb5b42d9128ee85fca39a2b545d0aa12a5248a203","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["58499b816234d2870950a2d6ef29c2c967cb1f3ccb0f51442708173dddfdcc9d","8054810094b905fbb6fb81ba3bed2e6c0e0103da6d6d64d607480334931bdc00","fc4674d6e47bda61464630ff9eabe1fb4c5adfd5505896144d785b7b656a5664","da3ad2c9b3be869795509372edb593c9a2bac75b8593db8f3176c0d891d4203d","4b288f446491a2f532ab6c048fe45595db1f624a0f6f89ccbb9b25736f31165b","b68137950a21ff2f26a70b91c8cf09b013726b661a844094dcf8f73aba5a9f4e","7da05ca2c6110f1480262723030b42162cb5aadf4f82a76f291569548047532b","c5b43e232a098f411bbe1813cac46327eed3b0658ef1d98a85bac65e7efa5c98","4e1e38549419919515122acc6996efde3bd1c4a9c3f28c3ded3347d2efe51c8d","5fa67ff5f45ecf7c197d3a30842b7146a9278273364fe53504a3ebd1d96eed7c","aa9f2e061ad3e4b3dec649c926911b3bf4c9a19be60b71bf5369c9f01e021371","21266513c1f7331df4698ac09b86a3019c20f697c3b879236a86b0f01e6adf2b","2d4ba48e8467086505fa67b0e9b912255ed8cfee1cdba70ccdc9e72637f5b68b","e53c2bb79e9018f6b707dfe427048c7255cc9dc338abc5e41198c5f729b9da26","598c237042b43d1c3e7f011f3e0083bf92dc76b0d70d3f169bd00e6db6ec1ea1","fd190c47d82de619e0dea15c852c69d7d2d5fe54b5f4dcd04068eabe09ce3658","71b93ca601fe3fec9b04f1e1ab3b790a6bd804bd77d5694feb98c3cd57ae008b","78696876cf3e95f672e7f304cec973c76e30dc5e6aadca8a371ffe68971ba3d2","651353c