{"body":{"actor":"w4","audit_root":"9ff1a65afd1225f6f698be91b5c9f99366ae5564ff7dd28acde72608b49b57ab","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T55-46d3e2e9623b14d1","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Clients and servers can maintain backwards compatibility with the deprecated [HTTP+SSE\ntransport](/specification/2024-11-05/basic/transports#http-with-sse) (from\nprotocol version 2024-11-05) as follows:","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o1","terms":["HTTP+SSE transport","backwards compatibility","deprecation"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"- Continue to host both the SSE and POST endpoints of the old transport, alongside the\n  new \"MCP endpoint\" defined for the Streamable HTTP transport.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o2","terms":["server endpoints","backwards compatibility","Streamable HTTP"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"  - It is also possible to combine the old POST endpoint and the new MCP endpoint, but\n    this may introduce unneeded complexity.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o3","terms":["combining endpoints","complexity","POST endpoint"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"   - If it fails with an HTTP 4xx status code (e.g., 405 Method Not Allowed or 404 Not\n     Found):","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o4","terms":["HTTP 4xx","fallback negotiation","client compatibility"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"     - When the `endpoint` event arrives, the client can assume this is a server running\n       the old HTTP+SSE transport, and should use that transport for all subsequent\n       communication.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o5","terms":["SSE endpoint event","HTTP+SSE transport","fallback"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Clients and servers **MAY** implement additional custom transport mechanisms to suit\ntheir specific needs.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o6","terms":["custom transports","MAY","optionality"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"The protocol is transport-agnostic and can be implemented over any\ncommunication channel that supports bidirectional message exchange.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o7","terms":["transport-agnostic","bidirectional message exchange"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Implementers who choose to support custom transports **MUST** ensure they preserve the\nJSON-RPC message format and lifecycle requirements defined by MCP.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o8","terms":["custom transports","MUST","JSON-RPC","lifecycle"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Custom transports\n**SHOULD** document their specific connection establishment and message exchange patterns\nto aid interoperability.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t55_o9","terms":["custom transports","SHOULD","interoperability","documentation"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t55_o1","t55_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t55_c1","object":"both legacy SSE and POST endpoints alongside the new MCP endpoint","predicate":"should host","stance":"qualified","subject":"servers supporting older clients","text":"Servers wishing to maintain compatibility with older clients should host both SSE and POST endpoints of the deprecated HTTP+SSE transport alongside the new MCP endpoint."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t55_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t55_c2","object":"unneeded complexity","predicate":"is possible but may introduce","stance":"qualified","subject":"combining old POST and new MCP endpoints","text":"Combining the legacy POST endpoint and the new MCP endpoint is permitted but qualified as potentially introducing unneeded complexity."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t55_o4","t55_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t55_c3","object":"HTTP 4xx response to InitializeRequest","predicate":"falls back to GET SSE stream upon","stance":"qualified","subject":"client backwards compatibility negotiation","text":"Clients fallback to GET requests expecting an SSE endpoint event when InitializeRequest fails with HTTP 4xx, qualifying backwards compatibility negotiation."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t55_o6","t55_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t55_c4","object":"any bidirectional communication channel","predicate":"MAY be implemented over","stance":"qualified","subject":"custom transports","text":"Clients and servers MAY implement custom transports over any bidirectional communication channel because MCP is transport-agnostic."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t55_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t55_c5","object":"JSON-RPC message format and lifecycle requirements defined by MCP","predicate":"MUST preserve","stance":"reported","subject":"custom transport implementers","text":"Implementers of custom transports MUST preserve JSON-RPC message formats and lifecycle requirements defined by MCP."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t55_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t55_c6","object":"connection establishment and message exchange patterns","predicate":"SHOULD document","stance":"qualified","subject":"custom transport documentation","text":"Documentation of connection establishment and message exchange patterns for custom transports is qualified as a SHOULD recommendation rather than a MUST."},{"based_on":["t55_o1","t55_o2"],"falsifier":"A subsequent specification revision retaining HTTP+SSE backwards compatibility fallback as a permanent requirement.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t55_h1","text":"The backwards compatibility mechanism for HTTP+SSE is provisional and will be completely removed in later revisions once protocol version 2024-11-05 is obsoleted."},{"about":["backwards compatibility with HTTP+SSE transport"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t55_q1","needed":"check later revisions of the MCP transport specification for deprecation removal","text":"Will backwards compatibility support and client fallback procedures for the deprecated HTTP+SSE transport be revoked in future revisions?"},{"about":["custom transport documentation requirements"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t55_q2","needed":"check subsequent specification revisions for custom transport normative rules","text":"Will custom transport interoperability documentation requirements be tightened from SHOULD to MUST in later protocol revisions?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b"],"ranges":[["d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b",11806,13770]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"b827c4dc96225b2997e1f0adc0d4f0f29a321bcfd54a86af89238ecb45b0e477","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["514123387b0958ac8c19b11c3582a656a649c3f8d3acb41011ee77c4c616a1ad","dc6698142f811ab8cdea2888aedf13f8371a7147fabc698e4f3af752bc29bb75","9b95466b8c3b58f6728f3820ab1bfaa08604f642cf1f45a1bace208c99260f32"