{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"178c7ba624653a889e3055a6a1d70aa282bbb6518e75f5f4e16387aa442ce533","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"TR60-167c98e73799efd5","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"MCP uses JSON-RPC to encode messages. JSON-RPC messages **MUST** be UTF-8 encoded.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o1","terms":["JSON-RPC encoding","UTF-8 requirement"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"The protocol currently defines two standard transport mechanisms for client-server","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o2","terms":["standard transports","stdio","Streamable HTTP"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"It is also possible for clients and servers to implement","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o3","terms":["custom transports","pluggable"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Messages are delimited by newlines, and **MUST NOT** contain embedded newlines.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o4","terms":["stdio framing","newline delimiting"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"The server **MAY** write UTF-8 strings to its standard error (`stderr`) for logging","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o5","terms":["stderr logging","optional"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"The server **MUST NOT** write anything to its `stdout` that is not a valid MCP message.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o6","terms":["stdout purity","stdio"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Servers **MUST** validate the `Origin` header on all incoming connections to prevent DNS rebinding attacks","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o8","terms":["Origin validation","DNS rebinding"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Servers **SHOULD** implement proper authentication for all connections","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o9","terms":["authentication recommendation","Streamable HTTP security"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"If the server accepts the input, the server **MUST** return HTTP status code 202","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o12","terms":["202 Accepted","responses/notifications only"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"The SSE stream **SHOULD** eventually include one JSON-RPC _response_ per each","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o14","terms":["SSE response per request","SHOULD"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"Disconnection **SHOULD NOT** be interpreted as the client cancelling its request.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o15","terms":["disconnection","cancellation semantics"]},{"doc_id":"d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b","exact_quote":"To avoid message loss due to disconnection, the server **MAY** make the stream","kind":"observe","local_id":"t60_o16","terms":["resumability","optional"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t60_o1","t60_o2","t60_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t60_c1","object":"stdio and Streamable HTTP","predicate":"currently comprise two standard mechanisms plus custom pluggable ones","stance":"reported","subject":"transport mechanisms","text":"JSON-RPC messages MUST be UTF-8 encoded; the protocol currently defines two standard transports (stdio and Streamable HTTP), and custom pluggable transports are also possible."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t60_o4","t60_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t60_c2","object":"stdio transport","predicate":"MUST be newline-delimited with no embedded newlines and stdout/stdin restricted to valid MCP messages","stance":"reported","subject":"stdio message framing","text":"In stdio, messages are newline-delimited and MUST NOT contain embedded newlines; the server MUST NOT write non-MCP data to stdout and the client MUST NOT write non-MCP data to stdin."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t60_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t60_c3","object":"stderr","predicate":"MAY be written by server and MAY be captured, forwarded or ignored by client","stance":"reported","subject":"stderr logging in stdio","text":"The server MAY write UTF-8 strings to stderr for logging, and clients MAY capture, forward, or ignore that logging."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t60_o8","t60_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t60_c5","object":"incoming connections","predicate":"MUST validate Origin but only SHOULD implement authentication","stance":"reported","subject":"Streamable HTTP security","text":"Servers MUST validate the Origin header on all incoming connections to prevent DNS rebinding attacks, while implementing proper authentication for all connections is only a SHOULD."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t60_o12"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t60_c7","object":"HTTP 202 Accepted or an HTTP error status","predicate":"MUST receive","stance":"reported","subject":"responses/notifications-only POST input","text":"If input is solely responses or notifications and the server accepts it, the server MUST return HTTP 202 Accepted with no body; otherwise it MUST return an HTTP error status."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t60_o14"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t60_c9","object":"JSON-RPC responses","predicate":"SHOULD eventually include one response per request, MAY be batched","stance":"reported","subject":"SSE stream responses","text":"An SSE stream SHOULD eventually include one JSON-RPC response per request sent in the POST body; these responses MAY be batched."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t60_o15"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t60_c10","object":"CancelledNotification","predicate":"SHOULD NOT imply cancellation; cancellation SHOULD use","stance":"reported","subject":"disconnection and cancellation","text":"Disconnection SHOULD NOT be interpreted as the client cancelling its request; to cancel, the client SHOULD explicitly send an MCP CancelledNotification."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t60_o16"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t60_c11","object":"server","predicate":"MAY be provided by","stance":"open","subject":"stream resumability","text":"To avoid message loss due to disconnection, the server MAY make the stream resumable; resumability is optional rather than required."},{"based_on":["t60_o14","t60_o15","t60_o16"],"falsifier":"A later revision of this section stating these MAY/SHOULD items as unconditional MUST requirements without change.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t60_h1","text":"The section's resumability and SSE-stream rules are normative but leave optionality (MAY/SHOULD) that later revisions could tighten or qualify."},{"based_on":["t60_o8","t60_o9"],"falsifier":"A later revision stating authentication as a MUST without change, or explicitly declaring the SHOULD final.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t60_h2","text":"Because authentication for Streamable HTTP connections is only a SHOULD while Origin validation is a MUST, the authentication requirement is a candidate for later tightening."},{"about":["t60_o9","t60_o14","t60_o16"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t60_q1","needed":"Check later revisions of the Transports section for changed requirement strengths.","text":"Does a later revision tighten the MAY/SHOULD items (resumability, SSE response-per-request, authentication) into MUST requirements?"},{"about":["t60_o3"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t60_q2","needed":"Check whether the custom-transports section defines conformance requirements.","text":"Are custom pluggable transports specified anywhere, or left entirely to implementers?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b"],"ranges":[["d_4bc9c307374945cef1fa7bdb9143f1965e53a345ab1ed3bf2b06f2510e14915b",0,5820]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"1479c38e8c2f952312eb15d500b261d2af9e83964b87f523ba0c135d3975ca3f","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["a75c8de9b50448aab710b467ac414fa863b8c30813b0414ee5825e2185df2bca","1e14d2dc1c79ec730674d3ad0a95eb42878cd53126d8931eab22a055f7a88166","47c197d3d0729d67c3c6aa70bfbc71cc1f101d54a2ee636614e031b6c2f5633a","cdb5d700c6b6f8d7a02685cbc9c1fb3da72b6aa52e49350b90492101e167f917","bd6cbcd8f81f5b5656e121b9ffc5adb7c0892282521f8bec590424f34379d93c","47c2da590b4c5df9e30fa9df4641948302b8ab152a1a2de3909ed2fe5394a09d","aa459786db6e4f4bc7714381b404f1cd6b3ebe1c3595f80a6d9a8e1bae77307f","6cf5b954031144bcad5b86a87aeddecc4d734ac61f4114566f587501f89ad1c5","c32811a7a6c898871598396595b39929bd8d2cbd6256bb1f8408440cd22246a5","833e87c7ba474cd9b06616c1f9939c0d881167760909c8cd40e147d18ef1dfbd","b1e55ac0b893d712156b48baf822905bcab65ba4d1cda36af2cb9d327a263d19","d14523cd4d173f7a0cfa87a9fa9f6606e597b1142a04426782a083b1034420f2","5f66020334444f5735a6ab2ab81ead2cf1e079f1c73872cff53d0cc13052bb07","898285da9618e112caad28b96a568e8896d2dc31625de801c82b20be523ffbbf","98f7a54aea9829a9eb7aa1a5b29a7a12b54ca636aeb7ecf69ea1cae57d2a2630","c0386d2