of the client or server, and **SHOULD NOT**\n  rely on them for security decisions.","suggested_span":{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","end_byte":20475,"start_byte":20328}},"field":"exact_quote","message":"a quote keeps the clause it belongs to: quote from the start of the sentence when it negates what follows, and to the end of the clause when the quote ends on a word like 'from' or 'with'","obligation":null,"status":"error"},"index":2,"local_id":"t61_o3"},{"error":{"code":"BAD_FIELD","expected_by_kernel":{"exact_bytes_in_section":"the server **MUST** include `io.modelcontextprotocol/subscriptionId` in `_meta` so the\nclient can correlate the notification with the originating subscription request.","rule":"ends_mid_clause","suggested_exact_quote":"the server **MUST** include `io.modelcontextprotocol/subscriptionId` in `_meta` so the\nclient can correlate the notification with the originating subscription request.","suggested_span":{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa631a415f80aa23eb","end_byte":20740,"start_byte":20573},"trailing_word":"the"},"field":"exact_quote","message":"a quote keeps the clause it belongs to: quote from the start of the sentence when it negates what follows, and to the end of the clause when the quote ends on a word like 'from' or 'with'","obligation":null,"status":"error"},"index":3,"local_id":"t61_o4"},{"error":{"code":"BAD_FIELD","expected_by_kernel":{"exact_bytes_in_section":"This exception exists to maintain compatibility with existing implementations and\n[OpenTelemetry semantic conventions for MCP](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/gen-ai/mcp/).","rule":"ends_mid_clause","suggested_exact_quote":"This exception exists to maintain compatibility with existing implementations and\n[OpenTelemetry semantic conventions for MCP](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/gen-ai/mcp/).","suggested_span":{"doc_id":"d_68a9337c46c31a3f0e9eafcca98f89260dc7a424155fdeaa6