e the most specific URI that they can for the MCP server they intend to access","kind":"observe","local_id":"t66_o5","terms":["canonical URI","SHOULD","specificity"]},{"doc_id":"d_75c650256ff6f4b1aae9eed534d15874767a71fb43d85848301cad48e7055546","exact_quote":"implementations **SHOULD** accept uppercase scheme and host components for robustness and interoperability.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t66_o6","terms":["canonical URI","uppercase","SHOULD"]},{"doc_id":"d_75c650256ff6f4b1aae9eed534d15874767a71fb43d85848301cad48e7055546","exact_quote":"implementations **SHOULD** consistently use the form without the trailing slash for better interoperability","kind":"observe","local_id":"t66_o7","terms":["trailing slash","SHOULD","interoperability"]},{"doc_id":"d_75c650256ff6f4b1aae9eed534d15874767a71fb43d85848301cad48e7055546","exact_quote":"Note over C,A: OAuth 2.1 authorization flow happens here","kind":"observe","local_id":"t66_o8","terms":["OAuth 2.1","deferred flow","sequence diagram"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t66_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t66_c2","object":"alternative ways to obtain a client ID","predicate":"need to provide","stance":"reported","subject":"authorization servers not supporting Dynamic Client Registration","text":"Authorization servers without Dynamic Client Registration must offer alternative client ID acquisition; clients then hardcode credentials or present a registration UI."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t66_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t66_c3","object":"Resource Indicators for OAuth 2.0 (RFC 8707)","predicate":"MUST implement","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP clients","text":"MCP clients MUST implement RFC 8707 Resource Indicators, including the resource parameter in authorization and token requests."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t66_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t66_c4","object":"authorization server support","predicate":"MUST be sent regardless of","stance":"open","subject":"resource parameter","text":"Clients MUST send the resource parameter regardless of whether authorization servers support it, leaving AS-side support open."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t66_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t66_c5","object":"MCP clients","predicate":"SHOULD provide most specific URI by","stance":"qualified","subject":"canonical server URI selection","text":"Clients SHOULD provide the most specific canonical server URI they can, per RFC 8707 guidance."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t66_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t66_c6","object":"implementations","predicate":"SHOULD be accepted by","stance":"qualified","subject":"uppercase scheme and host components","text":"Implementations SHOULD accept uppercase scheme and host components for robustness and interoperability."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t66_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t66_c7","object":"implementations","predicate":"SHOULD be omitted by","stance":"qualified","subject":"trailing slash in canonical URIs","text":"Implementations SHOULD consistently use canonical URIs without trailing slash unless the slash is semantically significant."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t66_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t66_c8","object":"unspecified external specification","predicate":"is deferred to","stance":"open","subject":"OAuth 2.1 authorization flow","text":"The OAuth 2.1 authorization flow itself is deferred in the diagram rather than specified in this section."},{"based_on":["t66_o4","t66_o8"],"falsifier":"A later revision specifying authorization server handling of the resource parameter within this document.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t66_h2","text":"Because clients MUST send resource regardless of AS support, conformance depends on authorization server behavior left unspecified here."},{"about":["dynamic client registration","resource parameter","authorization server"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t66_q1","needed":"Check later revisions of this authorization section for MUST-level DCR and AS resource handling.","text":"Does any later revision mandate Dynamic Client Registration or specify AS-side resource parameter support?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_75c650256ff6f4b1aae9eed534d15874767a71fb43d85848301cad48e7055546"],"ranges":[["d_75c650256ff6f4b1aae9eed534d15874767a71fb43d85848301cad48e7055546",5211,11199]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"3adbf70d51789ef2cd00688e316cccef3da7a16932d94ef930a6f77384468cfe","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["575d7215f08212eeb82ee5f2d13242f48ccaba4e7127faff5deb7453ab8b186c","ff87c34ad388d838538bb17878e73a41addea7dd6c4bf12f1936a6dbba13fb70","33b47bb39a1428bcfbb59e200500e3edbfd1cde77dab048a11d7908fb007281d","4c8f59a845bd114aa7ed9609a4a6ad8ddb00d333e5e13f7cedf57dff97b4d0a8","8ffba189fdc302f79f4563139d82c06ec2ac8473174fb61e384707c5a0f1f06c","2aae2a62abe17c5dee8238b28a25fc2288b8af096d6b8ada6c483c9c715d1a15","bcfb6c2a76e50f3c5749219ebeb8ef77053a17a17c6b2ea4125492b6cd090c59","6043b8ec5a9db95010829da7d6d7fbaceeb53c1c17197c0d19e2a2161491eb1e","b64a60128030f9f42cee53391429be6aac35a9550ec65d53bde67d7752145ad5","b51ea3ebcbc6f0ccd99b13759602811101b04d3882119d5b7b63644dc7e40cc6","66e3f61f70e986b666073db90c4001531b0d3924a4524d482b8fa55c81d4d3f2","c67100c2c231cad3b8d91989e50ca05d959e27f8c6b0091a6a97345c674c03f9","ca05a70993bea7516a424794974f919d47fa981b674a40a2996bc66e779d2554","bbf6e8ba3592424df6003dc2c2b2df3d8afe3ff88aaed266c26676fef5b5af7e","6ec46e7aad932a2bb0223c5e18d144363d4902b8dcc692d10d50423d55dcf382","3d11c74ecfb7129c602afc22d65054f83f098036dbb9f3ab71a700c34856b749"],"error":null,"failed_index":null}},"request_hash":"d804e36ed1f4e8ae9c474eaa7b90bf5c4bbdbdefa67b2cd7cc621fd1b8a58a36","submission_id":"T66-5ccc38d68626a2cb#1"},"hash":"c68637d8cf5cb2fadc05e291baae1b7254ea47430ed4c85ba87bd03b0051af00","header":{"body_hash":"65facd746b1e0e3543231efcfdc539c68f21e7dda604fb27d5afebd181e948b3","format":"sbgk-session-log/3","previous":"dd2ddf31c91621a25a25003e3e109b1dc41333b034a22459902548a3e3bbcbfd","records_root":"81578cd7cc0ab5a1a17c9c4508cb0d8cfec6502ea4039f46fffa76b6f74e6f8c","seq":320,"wal_op":"a