t69_o6","terms":["HTTP protocol version header","MUST","subsequent requests"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t69_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t69_c1","object":"client-server connection","predicate":"MUST be the first interaction, initiated by client with initialize request","stance":"reported","subject":"initialization phase","text":"The initialization phase MUST be the first interaction between client and server, and the client MUST initiate it with an initialize request."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t69_o4","t69_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t69_c3","object":"initialize request/response","predicate":"MUST send a supported version; latest-version preference and disconnect are SHOULD","stance":"reported","subject":"protocol version negotiation","text":"Version negotiation is normative for the version field but the 'latest version' choices are only SHOULD, and a client that cannot support the server's version SHOULD disconnect."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t69_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t69_c4","object":"HTTP transport requests","predicate":"MUST be included by client on subsequent requests","stance":"reported","subject":"MCP-Protocol-Version HTTP header","text":"When using HTTP, the client MUST include the MCP-Protocol-Version header on all subsequent requests to the MCP server."},{"about":["version negotiation","initialization request restrictions"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t69_q1","needed":"Check later revisions of the Lifecycle section for changed requirement keywords.","text":"Does any later revision tighten the SHOULD-level version negotiation and pre-initialization request restrictions into MUST requirements?"},{"about":["tasks capability","stability"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t69_q2","needed":"Check the tasks feature section and changelog for stability labeling.","text":"Is the tasks capability in the initialize examples marked experimental or stable elsewhere in the specification?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_7a1bf6bc8d125d79e704fa29cde580d628f34c