{"body":{"actor":"w4","audit_root":"21d992e09575c63e9d13a7533da9919483f38c936662153e678e2ea3abebf31f","command":{"allowed_records":["0c885f8470b25ebc51ca36f0f4f71018d6629a236e1f6a39a44d0602f73e5234","30b42a7ab9212b145c26f8c3152765d0ba3af8c5c020549baecd1d39ce47c3f4","30d75310ba2bad3440c9def6f6c7440e10fb0f2207a2e4b6988cb09b04e3db91","399b4b685f545ff205588b497f5477cb14da443874d8c3bf084e061f8a65e49a","3a2f36073d683624bd9f06eef7e4a1fa227212e198efbf74274040a652e4c6ff","63ce29418b3e97097f4c4bbaa7d41fe413c01a8b153b1416b04ba6a71f5e028b","6ca6665902277bc7a80dca0e5b2f93e1864409a7c11629686cc7bebe27acca7d","76f502a4467387cf1b20986139e5b7161f6c6ec4bf2369089e98440ac3fe68a8","8599201b97088cc4f0ffaade38e4e5019522853c782930f3cd8c6b365549c2fa","b57ad2fc70004f64ca8630d261d42642ea3533a01cbd708cbc2b8c0c3755afb4","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","f9b13ccee8f191b798c3d14c9931c1efc4ca0b830a1b81f22055d85becb402bd"],"directive":"T75-6bceca024b2d5860","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"1. Servers **MUST** validate the `Origin` header on all incoming connections to prevent DNS rebinding attacks","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o1","terms":["Origin header validation","DNS rebinding attacks"]},{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"3. Servers **SHOULD** implement proper authentication for all connections","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o2","terms":["server authentication","HTTP with SSE"]},{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"- Messages are delimited by newlines, and **MUST NOT** contain embedded newlines.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o3","terms":["stdio message delimitation","embedded newlines"]},{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"- The server **MUST NOT** write anything to its `stdout` that is not a valid MCP message.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o4","terms":["stdio stdout constraint","valid MCP message"]},{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"- The server **MAY** write UTF-8 strings to its standard error (`stderr`) for logging\n  purposes. Clients **MAY** capture, forward, or ignore this logging.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o5","terms":["stdio stderr logging","client logging handling"]},{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"When a client connects, the server **MUST** send an `endpoint` event containing a URI for\nthe client to use for sending messages.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o6","terms":["SSE endpoint event","URI announcement"]},{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"All subsequent client messages **MUST** be sent\nas HTTP POST requests to this endpoint.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o7","terms":["HTTP POST messages","SSE client communication"]},{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"Implementers who choose to support custom transports **MUST** ensure they preserve the\nJSON-RPC message format and lifecycle requirements defined by MCP.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o8","terms":["custom transports","JSON-RPC format preservation","lifecycle requirements"]},{"doc_id":"d_87097a7e9c2a6535d99d509ecd6237f2d5367adaad4d8d671bb78cf55dc3535b","exact_quote":"Custom transports\n**SHOULD** document their specific connection establishment and message exchange patterns\nto aid interoperability.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t75_o9","terms":["custom transports documentation","interoperability"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c1","object":"Origin header on all incoming connections","predicate":"MUST validate","stance":"reported","subject":"HTTP with SSE servers","text":"Servers implementing HTTP with SSE transport MUST validate the Origin header on all incoming connections to prevent DNS rebinding attacks."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c2","object":"servers","predicate":"SHOULD be implemented by","stance":"qualified","subject":"proper authentication for HTTP with SSE connections","text":"Proper authentication for HTTP with SSE connections is qualified as a recommendation (SHOULD) rather than an unconditional mandate."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c3","object":"embedded newlines","predicate":"MUST NOT contain","stance":"reported","subject":"stdio transport messages","text":"Messages in the stdio transport are delimited by newlines and MUST NOT contain embedded newlines."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c4","object":"anything that is not a valid MCP message","predicate":"MUST NOT contain","stance":"reported","subject":"stdio server standard output","text":"In the stdio transport, the server MUST NOT write anything to standard output that is not a valid MCP message."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c5","object":"clients","predicate":"MAY be written by server and MAY be handled by","stance":"qualified","subject":"stdio stderr logging","text":"Stdio stderr logging by the server is optional (MAY), and clients MAY capture, forward, or ignore this logging."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c6","object":"endpoint event containing a URI for sending messages","predicate":"MUST send upon client connection","stance":"reported","subject":"HTTP with SSE server","text":"In HTTP with SSE, upon client connection the server MUST send an endpoint event containing a URI for sending client messages."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c7","object":"HTTP POST requests to the endpoint URI","predicate":"MUST be sent as","stance":"reported","subject":"subsequent client messages in HTTP with SSE","text":"In HTTP with SSE, all subsequent client messages MUST be sent as HTTP POST requests to the endpoint provided by the server."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c8","object":"JSON-RPC message format and lifecycle requirements defined by MCP","predicate":"MUST preserve","stance":"reported","subject":"custom transports","text":"Implementers supporting custom transports MUST preserve the JSON-RPC message format and lifecycle requirements defined by MCP."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t75_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t75_c9","object":"connection establishment and message exchange patterns","predicate":"SHOULD document","stance":"qualified","subject":"documentation for custom transports","text":"Documenting specific connection establishment and message exchange patterns for custom transports is qualified as a recommendation (SHOULD)."},{"about":["HTTP with SSE authentication","proper authentication"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t75_q1","needed":"Check subsequent specifications or revisions for whether authentication requirements were tightened from SHOULD to MUST.","text":"What specific authentication schemes satisfy the recommendation that HTTP with SSE servers SHOULD implement proper authentication?"},{"about":["HTTP with SSE endpoint event","Streamable HTTP"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t75_q2","needed":"Check Streamable HTTP transport specification to confirm obsolescence of the separate endpoint event mechanism.","text":"Were the endpoint event and separate HTTP POST endpoint requirements superseded when HTTP with SSE was replaced by Streamable HTTP?"},{"about":["custom transports","interoperability"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t75_q3","needed":"Check later revisions for normative specifications or tests for pluggable custom transports.","text":"Are there standardized connection establishment or message exchange profiles defined for custom transports beyond the SHOULD guidance?"}],"scope":{"d