{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"fa76b065ad786fe8fbef2d8b4e51c29b8f70146b1e1525947e748ad5474422de","command":{"allowed_records":["6c00363611b38accc268752e90dc584a835f275b6a3c4342ec34ee1648f4206e","950869c850155a385df58b5b7931110600e6763fd48597f777b954ce4ef775ba"],"directive":"TQ96-6ddee2c654c9e38f","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"This section covers handling insufficient scope errors during runtime operations when","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o1","terms":["scope challenge handling","runtime insufficient scope"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"- `scope=\"required_scope1 required_scope2\"` - specifying the minimum scopes needed for the operation","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o2","terms":["WWW-Authenticate scope parameter","minimum scopes"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"**Server Scope Management**: When responding with insufficient scope errors, servers","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o3","terms":["server scope management","insufficient scope response"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"- **Recommended approach**: Include both existing relevant scopes and newly required scopes to prevent clients from losing previously granted permissions","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o4","terms":["recommended scope inclusion","existing plus new scopes"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Clients **SHOULD** respond to these errors by requesting a new access token with an increased set of scopes via a step-up authorization flow or handle the errors in other, appropriate ways.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o5","terms":["step-up authorization flow","client response"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"2. **Determine required scopes** as outlined in [Scope Selection Strategy](#scope-selection-strategy).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o6","terms":["step-up flow step 2","scope selection strategy reference"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"4. **Retry the original request** with the new authorization no more than a few times and treat this as a permanent authorization failure","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o7","terms":["retry limit","permanent authorization failure"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"Clients **SHOULD** implement retry limits and **SHOULD** track scope upgrade attempts to avoid","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o8","terms":["retry limits","scope upgrade tracking"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"with additional scopes requested incrementally through the step-up authorization flow steps","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o9","terms":["incremental scope requests","step-up flow"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"1. **Use `scope` parameter** from the initial `WWW-Authenticate` header in the 401 response, if provided","kind":"observe","local_id":"t96o10","terms":["scope selection priority","initial WWW-Authenticate scope"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t96o1","t96o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t96c1","object":"incremental scope requests","predicate":"SHOULD respond with 403 and WWW-Authenticate insufficient_scope plus scope","stance":"qualified","subject":"server response to runtime insufficient scope errors","text":"For incremental scope requests, the Scope Challenge Handling section specifies servers SHOULD answer runtime insufficient-scope requests with HTTP 403 and a Bearer WWW-Authenticate header carrying error=\"insufficient_scope\" and a scope parameter of minimum required scopes."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t96o3","t96o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t96c2","object":"scope parameter of insufficient_scope response","predicate":"SHOULD include needed scopes; recommended approach adds existing relevant scopes","stance":"qualified","subject":"server scope inclusion strategy in insufficient scope responses","text":"Servers SHOULD include the scopes needed to satisfy the current request in the scope parameter, choosing among minimum, recommended (existing relevant plus newly required), or extended inclusion, and SHOULD be consistent."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t96o5","t96o6","t96o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t96c3","object":"incremental scope requests","predicate":"SHOULD perform; steps: parse, determine scopes, re-authorize, retry limited","stance":"qualified","subject":"client step-up authorization flow for incremental scopes","text":"Clients SHOULD respond to scope errors by requesting a new token with an increased scope set via step-up authorization or other appropriate handling; the flow parses error info, determines scopes per Scope Selection Strategy, re-authorizes, and retries a few times."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t96o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t96c4","object":"step-up authorization attempts","predicate":"SHOULD implement and track","stance":"qualified","subject":"client retry limits and scope upgrade tracking","text":"Clients SHOULD implement retry limits and track scope upgrade attempts to avoid repeated failures for the same resource and operation combination."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t96o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t96c5","object":"additional scopes beyond scopes_supported","predicate":"are made through step-up authorization flow steps in Scope Challenge Handling","stance":"reported","subject":"incremental scope requests","text":"The Scope Selection Strategy states additional scopes beyond scopes_supported are requested incrementally through the step-up authorization flow steps described in Scope Challenge Handling."},{"about":["scope priority rules","step-up scope determination"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t96q1","needed":"Compare Scope Selection Strategy priority order with Step-Up Authorization Flow step 2 and Runtime Insufficient Scope scope parameter in the authorization spec.","text":"Does the Scope Challenge Handling section's step 2 (determine required scopes per Scope Selection Strategy) mean the initial-handshake priority order (WWW-Authenticate scope, else scopes_supported) applies to step-up, or does the insufficient_scope response's scope parameter take precedence?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54"],"ranges":[["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54",14801,19354],["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54",24431,30038]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"2e30fdc066adc4ebf078503cc2fc1b9681afd8c6f86a38ae4d84bb0e0a2c8bdf","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["a6a83ccc31dc8efe3cb08a146b7921d95e2132b0fd537f50572a868c381fbe58","1e40e3737983884f6ebf5a9f932b0e775527dc13ffc70462fc1fb25927349fe4","d1a7748df2d7bbd2b72bc6f33a947da99041776faaebd9701517e8b3c80ffa97","d628b3c0346bd1be1fed7c98b9a6dc6ef918a7f23cad6483ab9df54e42215098","b0f08c8972385b76ebeb584c37f108f77f59d7caa4106c4b1ce3f76cf5155d6c","9e53135763f8830242bad823bdd7974587f7b7912e56856132a4d729b4f51551","698ef2194e7dad6e865b373934743830bb82a0093c66c7673c9ef284a4351950","bfddc01cea238bd4a918325631dd3ab6f4a8bb1743a82a4a41d1a1e6a6e6b4e5","aa2668324a1bbc30288384284a255076bd6f63a9df5653ee93b85d174aad90c0","21c9ba5910e5f9db053f2d6cc97c3a92c63d594b9e2dd8a368a2a3f9e5478b9e"],"error":{"code":"BAD_FIELD","expected_by_kernel":{"maxLength":240,"minLength":1,"type":"string","x-maxUtf8Bytes":1024},"field":"text","message":"'text' is empty or exceeds its character/UTF-8 byte bound","obligation":null,"status":"error"},"failed_index":10}},"request_hash":"7dc12f660d42ce906377163c77360841bd927cec7fbee904de6c8f06a66b3d3f","subm