event arrives, the client can assume this is a server running","kind":"observe","local_id":"t92_o5","terms":["client detects old HTTP+SSE server via endpoint event"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"Revision 2026-07-28 changed the behavior of Streamable HTTP. Clients must","kind":"observe","local_id":"t92_o6","terms":["revision 2026-07-28 changes Streamable HTTP and requires backwards-compatibility handling"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"Removal of the GET stream endpoint.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t92_o7","terms":["removal of GET stream endpoint in 2026-07-28"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t92_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t92_c2","object":"possible but may add unneeded complexity","predicate":"is","stance":"reported","subject":"combined old POST endpoint and new MCP endpoint","text":"Combining the old POST endpoint with the new MCP endpoint is possible but may introduce unneeded complexity."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t92_o4","t92_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t92_c3","object":"old HTTP+SSE transport once endpoint event arrives","predicate":"should use","stance":"reported","subject":"client fallback after HTTP 4xx from InitializeRequest POST","text":"A client whose InitializeRequest POST fails with HTTP 4xx issues a GET and, on receiving an endpoint event, uses the old HTTP+SSE transport."},{"as_of":20260728,"based_on":["t92_o6","t92_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t92_c5","object":"GET stream endpoint; clients must handle backwards compatibility","predicate":"changed behavior and removed","stance":"reported","subject":"Streamable HTTP in revision 2026-07-28","text":"Revision 2026-07-28 changed Streamable HTTP, requires clients to handle backwards compatibility, and removes the GET stream endpoint."},{"about":["legacy HTTP+SSE client sending requests to MCP endpoint","Streamable HTTP backwards compatibility"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t92_q1","needed":"Check the Backward Compatibility subsection of the Streamable HTTP page (d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530, the #backward-compatibility anchor), which is not in the shown text, and the 2024-11-05 transports page for legacy client behavior.","text":"How does a server answer a legacy HTTP+SSE client that sends its InitializeRequest or GET to the single MCP endpoint instead of the old SSE and POST endpoints?"},{"about":["GET fallback for old servers","removed GET stream endpoint in 2026-07-28"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t92_q2","needed":"Check the Backward Compatibility subsection and the 2026-07-28 changelog linked from d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530; neither is in the shown text.","text":"Does removal of the GET stream endpoint in revision 2026-07-28 break the client fallback that issues a GET to the server URL expecting an endpoint event?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530"],"ranges":[["d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b",11113,13956],["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530",0,4380]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"31c9d4d48b807eefb5bca38c322dffdabf9e61c6959fe9762f6a7c05e00488e1","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["3b88099678320d7cfaa2ec6a9b39acb23501852b0c1d2fe1339e7a0998aa2a7a","149e71b6a1d34664c78900a3b8e4ffbcb7f0208f3f392b1868d94d9d4ada9f59","510e0230c4ed326594668852c92e6dd55e0a31da242e26bec8a2a71a33fe9516","a492171153c47b202681618f7c4ca568c110016685cbe591fc17c3622f7feb6a","93fe1d2c2a2516361c66193058c0002c63e5d43f9cb3a75f68cf3ca3be9b517b","7784b6906fd5ce057e00148e2914abbe7e4233d8909b2c07930d5eb2875ee155","f62f7ac9894ea6336ddc981fd3baedcf6a9786f99cb4a80013e5e5cc38e1295a","f83860271166c02a57e6d1a30ade3c6de1071ea3190beb86d606cfe9aa83ba19","1e5caf3153788ab3ebf99d803b6e4bf6c5a