{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"a50f96d9881ffaf7ee2c9f959ae029d4d2e91008c66d284778e7277bfb87a4b2","command":{"allowed_records":["1be4f3affb896e226a575da5b5f03b2d1b2083e28a48fa28046b38e8ad6bc1c2","2dddb3d9720f75340bff317d0bbb7b7c9d1943ce81e3708bc9d8bf6c0584b23a","4aca91d18f939f409a638d93054c7476935767d4068db0d5df2613e9567ddee0","4e8f55b1d865dcd9f1438659ffb36f93223ae42e057dcb35bc2db9bbd00c26d3","5a42ca58e9c15b6db21d90b908e7f65a9dd8d5ad76dab6766dd773820a5db98c","6b788fb63f91df83cb59fec6cf92ce8bf7702787a95952816f140db0f34f026c","78696876cf3e95f672e7f304cec973c76e30dc5e6aadca8a371ffe68971ba3d2","7be0d16197f48468293842d9e5d2011f353918ec27c5171e29955e95010a505f","7dd745a069b069736811b4a2886178607e0b279e3fff7f705f32e34283cb5c90","9b4e968da73e3a5bf18424c572e40d8bb160c4a551999c6e33f70fbaac57b522","bb4a5f59d822ad177ec3ce946ebe0b9bea40d6a0e6affa45895c672741758b02","e9c223a7b25ea9f0963e0be7bbb712838c0aca1befc0e4399b3a5af0b3d2ed3a"],"directive":"TQ102-2dfcd6ffc4744449","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_e78b49b5f4912f5115eb9b9dbd5b8785bf919e27b2c1bfd2e93e784e7ef9a936","exact_quote":"9. Remove SSE stream resumability and message redelivery (the `Last-Event-ID` header and SSE event IDs) from the Streamable HTTP transport.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t102_o1","terms":["Last-Event-ID removal","SSE resumability","message redelivery"]},{"doc_id":"d_e78b49b5f4912f5115eb9b9dbd5b8785bf919e27b2c1bfd2e93e784e7ef9a936","exact_quote":"A broken response stream loses the in-flight request; clients **MUST** re-issue it as a new request with a new request ID","kind":"observe","local_id":"t102_o2","terms":["broken stream recovery","re-issue request","new request ID"]},{"doc_id":"d_e78b49b5f4912f5115eb9b9dbd5b8785bf919e27b2c1bfd2e93e784e7ef9a936","exact_quote":"Replace the HTTP GET endpoint and `resources/subscribe`/`resources/unsubscribe` with `subscriptions/listen`","kind":"observe","local_id":"t102_o3","terms":["subscriptions/listen","HTTP GET endpoint removed"]},{"doc_id":"d_e78b49b5f4912f5115eb9b9dbd5b8785bf919e27b2c1bfd2e93e784e7ef9a936","exact_quote":"a single long-lived POST-response stream for opted-in server-to-client change notifications","kind":"observe","local_id":"t102_o4","terms":["subscriptions/listen stream","long-lived POST-response stream"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"If the client wishes to resume after a broken connection, it **SHOULD** issue an HTTP","kind":"observe","local_id":"t102_o5","terms":["resume after broken connection","HTTP GET"]},{"doc_id":"d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","exact_quote":"The server **MAY** use this header to replay messages that would have been sent","kind":"observe","local_id":"t102_o6","terms":["server replay optional","Last-Event-ID"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t102_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t102_c1","object":"the Streamable HTTP transport","predicate":"are removed from","stance":"confirmed","subject":"SSE stream resumability and message redelivery","text":"The 2026-07-28 revision removes SSE stream resumability and message redelivery, including the Last-Event-ID header and SSE event IDs, from the Streamable HTTP transport."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t102_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t102_c2","object":"a new request with a new request ID","predicate":"MUST be re-issued as","stance":"confirmed","subject":"in-flight request lost on broken response stream","text":"After a broken response stream loses the in-flight request, clients MUST re-issue it as a new request with a new request ID."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t102_o3","t102_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t102_c3","object":"subscriptions/listen POST-response stream","predicate":"is replaced by","stance":"confirmed","subject":"HTTP GET endpoint","text":"The HTTP GET endpoint is replaced by subscriptions/listen, a single long-lived POST-response stream for opted-in server-to-client change notifications."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t102_o5","t102_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t102_c4","object":"messages after last event ID on disconnected stream","predicate":"SHOULD issue HTTP GET with Last-Event-ID, server MAY replay","stance":"superseded","subject":"client resumption after broken connection","text":"In the earlier revision, a client wishing to resume after a broken connection SHOULD issue an HTTP GET with Last-Event-ID, and the server MAY replay messages after that ID on the disconnected stream only."},{"about":["subscriptions/listen reconnection","missed notification handling"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t102_q1","needed":"Check the subscriptions/listen and transport sections of the 2026-07-28 revision for reconnection, replay, or missed-notification rules; the Key Changes section only states resumability was removed.","text":"Does any section of the 2026-07-28 revision define how a client re-establishes a subscriptions/listen stream after disconnect, and whether missed notifications are replayed or lost?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b","d_e78b49b5f4912f5115eb9b9dbd5b8785bf919e27b2c1bfd2e93e784e7ef9a936"],"ranges":[["d_e78b49b5f4912f5115eb9b9dbd5b8785bf919e27b2c1bfd2e93e784e7ef9a936",0,4413],["d_1ec5d9d1465c47e1696aa6369bdc6582a4210481ce571922656ff4fa73cb170b",5241,11113]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"139e91fc4b735ba84d3e6e59f104a5949c2591ba98545b857f1b50b92940c153","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["4cae11dc48160c9ca8ff5f80704799ec754d3cfb25aeb163ff832b226fcaad1d","bb3286c85af663990f1bcf7776c47f6237b070fd41d8b6d5fb4f33d5438b423d","73c445a8e33a72265ed8ae3960346f7ef20bfe38c5c1cad9638cfbf729ab7668","23677c06b41abb0969ac5db8dffa2018e851f5e7a4d10458a9b2f88c334137c0","b83d179d511cab9302319ef8aba06400f7d2c5fda4d2a17534b6cd3f2a69342f","c31a12b16ef0bca00e20bf001cbede1bce3f90cf96e3c31aa71a0a134c801989","e046e7d2652356b4ab7779b8feafe2dbb7f656294ef15e747dfeded4869cfeba","07f86914dfc70742b2be9b0f8694eba26dfeff09450d5d6099d2e78