{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"389b98613ec684c2037ac4cd198afbccf0341e969453edaa0055565c41f167ba","command":{"allowed_records":["141cec82143891c1b964c2a61f91859f089dfcb3279c031ace976f383a123054","1a02ff75b07a933e13f61c57de95cbbd1c804328ebb6d7955770b60f951e748a","1cf380e48cd508e1dc7cb923ba4cf2daefc949c84811916d38973f75a17bf781","2b190d76a3de585caf8d7386795ef6c465978796118b04f52b71d8927fcafe87","46f905af2cfb26c7f82ed399bcc3d9af9a559ec7d5d263db7b16c4e83de437f0","4d513b329bace977b1a55498dd1c05d6faf83325bfa9be971c31d65fd57c36be","60aecb07ef49a3c9a68dfcadbe545068b11d0c859648b37328de517bf5a15469","b3aa3baef9920bcffde6ff29af341478b679f74f607187e8ed50232c256b840c"],"directive":"TQ108-ce992e1905961116","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"Fails. The server may reject the request with an implementation-defined error, stay silent, or even process an era-ambiguous method under legacy semantics.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t108_o1","terms":["modern client","legacy server","implementation-defined error","failure mode"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"stdio: the server rejects `initialize` with a JSON-RPC error; the exact code is implementation-defined","kind":"observe","local_id":"t108_o2","terms":["legacy client","modern server","initialize rejection","implementation-defined code"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"If the body is empty or is not a recognized modern JSON-RPC error, fall","kind":"observe","local_id":"t108_o3","terms":["fallback","error-code-agnostic detection","empty body"]},{"doc_id":"d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","exact_quote":"See [Versioning: Backward Compatibility][lifecycle-compat] for the era model","kind":"observe","local_id":"t108_o4","terms":["era model","compatibility matrix","deferred"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t108_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t108_c1","object":"implementation-defined error, silence, or legacy-semantics processing","predicate":"failure mode remains implementation-defined or ambiguous","stance":"confirmed","subject":"modern client with legacy server","text":"The compatibility matrix still leaves the modern-client/legacy-server outcome unpinned: implementation-defined error, silence, or legacy-semantics processing; only a SHOULD-level server/discover probe gives determinism."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t108_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t108_c2","object":"exact JSON-RPC error code","predicate":"initialize rejection code remains implementation-defined","stance":"confirmed","subject":"legacy client with modern server","text":"For a legacy client against a modern server on stdio, the initialize rejection's exact JSON-RPC error code is still stated as implementation-defined; no concrete code is given."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t108_o3","t108_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t108_c3","object":"recognized modern JSON-RPC error body; Versioning: Backward Compatibility","predicate":"is error-code-agnostic and defers era model","stance":"reported","subject":"legacy fallback detection","text":"The backward-compatibility section keys fallback on the body being empty or not a recognized modern JSON-RPC error, not on a specific code, and defers the era model and matrix to the Versioning page."},{"based_on":["t108_o1","t108_o2"],"falsifier":"A later revision or error-code registry in these sections naming a specific code for the initialize rejection or the modern-client/legacy-server failure.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t108_h1","text":"No later revision in these sections pins concrete error codes for either the legacy-client/modern-server initialize rejection or the modern-client/legacy-server failure mode; both remain implementation-defined."},{"about":["error-code registry","Versioning: Backward Compatibility","initialize rejection"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t108_q1","needed":"Check the Versioning: Backward Compatibility page and any JSON-RPC error-code registry for concrete codes replacing implementation-defined ones.","text":"Does the Versioning: Backward Compatibility page or any error-code registry name a concrete code for the legacy-client/modern-server initialize rejection or the modern-client/legacy-server failure?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530","d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa"],"ranges":[["d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa",5784,11293],["d_36ab192089a83fd6eabe54d7808ec33520aa72f22c33d5866c34b0aebcb7a530",26565,31155]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"f937eea4bfc06d5fb37bebf71da37f0dad05277a4a6c102d56e0df5085492f39","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["f6357922ffc13aa03afe884edae01a0f3057438831277b59b82902ea7a2f7238","8b1815485effa779f40e01ea1daed38cd06108285173ca852054c2d9aa9ca079","3a7a6847a7c2950f80cba801497e87b5ff723af20cace4b85fe5e6c9f2e75150","7ffd47d04b02102cbae2cdc09f7f4ee8f9c7bde7a95fc171a7ac445d4ac6051c","e0baf94b39359ab0f51dc8c96407b691c1b9a028bce10e34384b58242bfeebf2","68dab03d10f1712995879c8a926c6fd35ca3b5b04425ee68d957fb27f8d1a206","9d1c45842abc392a193d969640cfe7ed612b2d53ad0bd3b07ef4e93e5a6220b3","fbdf39e915b35d9d8cf8ce7f25a09d69eba018e31bcccae1f34dafd92725c256","b4007424f16c80024331ad5f987669f9d78b71b12f6abf77b7bcdb2d76179e44"],"error":null,"failed_index":null}},"request_hash":"496d7449db4cfba46a4a29d30a619bd883a61f052bf68e9e345809b24f13d9dc","submission_id":"TQ108-ce992e1905961116#1"},"hash":"c12c7b9afaf9245657098323f1dc96367c95f5db8aeb34d12a5f89daa19e4140","header":{"body_hash":"4961f8229730df4937787ea6a07ad40f0eb112d02ee7e990a74823e7692cc35f","format":"sbgk-session-log/3","previous":"db95d04a9bdd0abdaf9cd9d95281ba9096b0977ae37668d7f948b2265b63d8ec","records_root":"30f969775d5c3f8680be856f39abbfd78bfc47c6b5d7020b85ef327e263ef078","seq":522,"wal