,"kind":"observe","local_id":"t113_o4","terms":["insufficient_scope error code"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"- `scope=\"required_scope1 required_scope2\"` - specifying the minimum scopes needed for the operation","kind":"observe","local_id":"t113_o5","terms":["scope parameter","minimum scopes"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"- `resource_metadata` - the URI of the Protected Resource Metadata document (for consistency with 401 responses)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t113_o6","terms":["resource_metadata","RFC 9728 metadata URI"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"- `error_description` (optional) - human-readable description of the error","kind":"observe","local_id":"t113_o7","terms":["error_description","optional parameter"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"and leverages the metadata fields from [RFC 9728 (OAuth 2.0 Protected Resource Metadata)]","kind":"observe","local_id":"t113_o9","terms":["RFC 9728","metadata fields"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"1. **Parse error information** from the authorization server response or `WWW-Authenticate` header","kind":"observe","local_id":"t113_o10","terms":["step-up flow","parse error info"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t113_o1","t113_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t113_c1","object":"HTTP 403 Forbidden status code","predicate":"SHOULD be","stance":"reported","subject":"server response to runtime insufficient scope","text":"On runtime insufficient scope, the server SHOULD respond with HTTP 403 Forbidden per RFC 6750 Section 3.1."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t113_o3","t113_o4","t113_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t113_c2","object":"Bearer scheme with error=insufficient_scope and scope parameters","predicate":"SHOULD include","stance":"reported","subject":"WWW-Authenticate header on insufficient scope","text":"The 403 insufficient-scope response SHOULD carry a WWW-Authenticate Bearer header with error=\"insufficient_scope\" and a scope parameter listing minimum required scopes."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t113_o6","t113_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t113_c3","object":"URI of the RFC 9728 Protected Resource Metadata document","predicate":"is","stance":"reported","subject":"resource_metadata parameter in insufficient-scope challenge","text":"The insufficient-scope WWW-Authenticate header includes resource_metadata, the URI of the Protected Resource Metadata document, for consistency with 401 responses."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t113_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t113_c4","object":"optional human-readable description in the challenge","predicate":"is","stance":"reported","subject":"error_description parameter","text":"The insufficient-scope challenge may include an optional error_description parameter with a human-readable error description."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t113_o10"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t113_c6","object":"parsing WWW-Authenticate error information","predicate":"SHOULD begin by","stance":"reported","subject":"client step-up authorization flow","text":"Clients SHOULD respond to insufficient_scope errors by parsing error info from the WWW-Authenticate header and initiating step-up authorization with determined scopes."},{"about":["RFC 9728 metadata fields","scope challenge"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t113_q1","needed":"Check sections after Scope Challenge Handling for Protected Resource Metadata field definitions.","text":"Does any later section state the exact RFC 9728 field names (e.g., resource, authorization_servers, scopes_supported) that the resource_metadata document must expose for scope challenges?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","d_3bcac267170918a3c71fa359fb054f85c896015d8dbca609854b53c8