ol/ui"]},{"doc_id":"d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa","exact_quote":"[Tasks extension](/extensions/tasks/overview) identified as `io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks`","kind":"observe","local_id":"t124_o5","terms":["Tasks extension","io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"- **Versioned independently** - Extensions follow the core MCP versioning cycle but may adopt independent versioning as needed","kind":"observe","local_id":"t124_o6","terms":["authorization extensions","independent versioning"]},{"doc_id":"d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","exact_quote":"A list of supported extensions can be found in the [MCP Authorization Extensions](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-auth) repository.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t124_o7","terms":["authorization extensions list","ext-auth repository"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t124_o1","t124_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t124_c1","object":"_meta key naming rules with mandatory prefix","predicate":"MUST follow _meta naming rules and are specified per extension","stance":"reported","subject":"extension identifiers and settings schemas","text":"Extension identifiers MUST follow the _meta key naming rules with a mandatory prefix, and each extension specifies the schema of its settings object."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t124_o4","t124_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t124_c2","object":"io.modelcontextprotocol/ui and io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks","predicate":"are only exemplified by","stance":"qualified","subject":"official extension identifiers","text":"The extension-negotiation section names only io.modelcontextprotocol/ui (MCP Apps) and io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks (Tasks) as examples; it does not enumerate all official extensions or their _meta keys."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t124_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t124_c3","object":"extensions","predicate":"SHOULD be documented by","stance":"qualified","subject":"extension fallback behavior documentation","text":"Extensions SHOULD document their expected fallback behavior, so fallback documentation is recommended rather than mandated."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t124_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t124_c4","object":"independent versioning as needed","predicate":"may adopt","stance":"qualified","subject":"authorization extensions","text":"Authorization extensions follow the core MCP versioning cycle but may adopt independent versioning as needed, so their versioning cadence is not fixed to the core."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t124_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t124_c5","object":"the ext-auth repository","predicate":"are listed in","stance":"reported","subject":"supported authorization extensions","text":"The list of supported authorization extensions is external to the spec, in the MCP Authorization Extensions (ext-auth) repository."},{"about":["official extension _meta keys","extension stability","ext-auth repository"],"kind":"question","local_id":"t124_q1","needed":"Check each extension's documentation page (e.g. /extensions/apps/overview, /extensions/tasks/overview, ext-auth repo) for defined _meta keys and versioning statements; the two sections shown only exemplify two extensions and defer the list to the ext-auth repository.","text":"Which official extensions (beyond io.modelcontextprotocol/ui and io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks) define additional io.modelcontextprotocol/ _meta keys, and does each extension's own documentation state its versioning/stability?"}],"scope":{"docs":["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54","d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa"],"ranges":[["d_34f79fc515679e3aad5c296e9d9d5778e565fdf5e53b905d53c0850fb198fe54",35989,41363],["d_39bd634003813aff0451340f032539c02df334ef4f7b8a8958dbeef0bd1ee6aa",0,5784]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"30c52f13c42f579a8f7bb8635f1cfc54740dad15cfa3897dbafc5b0b6